// ROTATION IS A REFUSING STEP, NOT A RECORDED INTENTION (machine-intake design
// doc §6 and its discriminating control in §16: "Leave factory credential
// working after rotation | BmcSecure refuses"). The phase's required result is
// stated there as a CONJUNCTION over two independent readbacks — the unique
// managed credential works AND the published factory credential no longer
// works — and the second half is the one every ordinary rotation script drops:
// creating an account and getting a 201 back says nothing about whether the
// bootstrap login still opens a session. A phase that recorded only the first
// half would report BmcSecure satisfied on a machine that any reader of the
// vendor's published default can still log into, which is the
// fabricated-plausible-output failure of DESIGN §5 aimed at the one phase whose
// whole purpose is to close that door.
//
// This module owns the WORKFLOW STANDING of that conjunction. It observes
// nothing: extdeps.bmc owns the external shapes, the effectful rotation
// actuator owns the observation, and the fold below owns what a set of
// readbacks may and may not conclude. Its route to a consumer is
// bmc_secure_phase_receipt, whose envelope is read by
// gunbc.machine_intake.disposition.derive_fleet_admission exactly as every
// other phase's is; there is no second admission path for credentials.
//
// WHY THE VOCABULARY IS NOT gunbc.bmc.bmc_onboarding's. That module is quarantined
// legacy (machine-intake ruling 2026-08-29, answer (b)): its
// FactoryDefault -> CredentialsRotated progression ADVANCES ITSELF with pure
// functions and consumes no readback at all, so it cannot refuse. This is the
// BMC-security extraction the ruling's §14 names, and it imports nothing from
// that module by construction — the quarantine witness requires exactly that
// no name bridges the two.

// WHAT ONE AUTHENTICATION ATTEMPT ESTABLISHED. Three arms, and the third is
// not the second wearing a softer name: a probe that could not run proves
// nothing about whether the credential works. Reading Unestablished as
// Rejected is the absorbing fallback of DESIGN §5 applied to the exact place
// it does the most damage — an unreachable account service would silently
// certify that the published credential had been retired.
type CredentialProbeOutcome
  = CredentialAccepted { evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: EpochMs }
  | CredentialRejected { evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: EpochMs }
  | CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: NonEmptyStr }

fn credential_probe_evidence(outcome: CredentialProbeOutcome) -> EvidenceRef? {
  match outcome {
    CredentialAccepted { evidence: e, observed_at: _ } => Present { value: e }
    CredentialRejected { evidence: e, observed_at: _ } => Present { value: e }
    CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: _ } => none
  }
}

// THE RECEIPT NEVER CONTAINS THE PASSWORD, AND HAS NOWHERE TO PUT ONE (design
// §6). This is the durable half of a rotation: WHERE the credential lives and
// WHICH generation it is. There is no Secret-typed field on this record or on
// anything reachable from it, so redaction is unnecessary — the excluded state
// has no constructor (DESIGN §4b rung 4) rather than a validator that strips it.
//
// The location is a SecretRef because gunbc.secret_provision already owns where
// this fleet's secrets live (fleet_secret_ref); a fresh `secret_name: NonEmptyStr`
// beside it — which is what gunbc.bmc.bmc_onboarding's plan carries — is the second
// name for one concept DESIGN §3 forbids.
type ManagedCredentialReference {
  account: NonEmptyStr
  role: RedfishAccountRole
  secret: SecretRef
  credential_epoch: Int
}

// WHETHER THE ROTATION WAS APPLIED AT ALL, and when. applied_at is on the
// APPLICATION rather than beside it because the two readbacks below are only
// evidence about the rotation if they were taken after it; a rotation with no
// time has no ordering to check against, and the ordering is what stops a
// pre-rotation "the published credential was already rejected" reading from
// being replayed as the post-rotation proof.
//
// WHAT THE ORDERING DOES NOT ESTABLISH, said here so it is not read off the
// refusal names: these are times carried on SUPPLIED observations, so the fold
// enforces an ordering AMONG THE READINGS IT WAS HANDED and establishes nothing
// about whether any BMC was probed at all. That is the boundary DESIGN §4b
// keeps off the ladder — an external fact, observed at a declared frontier and
// never fabricated here. The frontier is the effectful rotation actuator that
// produces BmcCredentialRotationObservation; it does not exist yet, and it is
// the same producer the machine-intake ruling gates on the gunbc.bmc.bmc_onboarding
// split.
type CredentialRotationApplication
  = RotationApplied { reference: ManagedCredentialReference, applied_at: EpochMs, evidence: EvidenceRef }
  | RotationNotAttempted
  | AccountManagementUnavailable { detail: NonEmptyStr }

// ONE LAN PROBE, ADDRESSED TO ONE CENSUS MEMBER. The join matches when BOTH
// channel and assigned IPv4 agree (DESIGN §5: completeness is an identity
// join, not a count, and not a disjunction). A probe that names the member's
// channel and a different address, or the member's address and a different
// channel, covers no member: a rejection observed at 9.9.9.9 cannot close
// 10.0.0.1. The old single published_probe minted BmcSecured while a second
// LAN address still accepted; a disjunctive key would reopen that arm.
type PublishedCredentialLanProbe {
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber
  address: Ipv4Address
  outcome: CredentialProbeOutcome
}

// HOW THE PUBLISHED ACCOUNT WOULD RETURN. Firmware reset is the MegaRAC
// residual measured on Mt. Collins unit 1: the disabled factory user remains
// on the controller and a firmware reset restores it. Administrator re-enable
// is the other documented restore, not a prose note.
type PublishedCredentialRestorePath
  = FirmwareResetRestoresPublishedAccount
  | AdministratorReEnableRestoresPublishedAccount

// A DELIBERATE BACKDOOR IS A NAMED POLICY OUTCOME, NEVER AN OPEN MACHINE.
// Break-glass is the default: a credential we own (SecretRef, never a
// password, never the published factory login). Keeping the published
// factory password is a separately named choice because that password is
// public and grants power, console, virtual media and firmware flash to
// anyone on the BMC network.
type RetainedCredentialKind
  = BreakGlassAccount { secret: SecretRef }
  | PublishedFactoryCredential

// THE PUBLISHED ACCOUNT'S STANDING ON THE CONTROLLER, independent of whether
// a LAN probe rejected. Rejected-on-LAN and deleted-from-the-user-list are
// different facts: a disabled user still exists, and BmcSecured must say so.
// observed_at is ordered against rotation applied_at in adjudicate_published_census
// (PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation); a pre-rotation user-list cannot
// label the post-rotation standing.
// RetainedByPolicy is a third arm: it satisfies the BMC-secure conjunct
// ONLY under a TestRisk-admitting policy. A ProdRisk-admitting policy refuses it; that refusal is the
// discriminating control for the day a machine is promoted.
type PublishedCredentialAccountObservation
  = PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: EpochMs }
  | PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired {
      restore_path: PublishedCredentialRestorePath
      evidence: EvidenceRef
      observed_at: EpochMs
    }
  | PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy {
      retention: RetainedCredentialKind
      evidence: EvidenceRef
      observed_at: EpochMs
    }

// THE OBSERVATION, BOUND TO ITS SUBJECT AND ITS CONTROLLER. sole_constructor
// keeps a caller from spelling the record beside the mint; it does not make the
// caller honest about where the readbacks came from, and this module does not
// claim it does. What it does hold is that the readings are carried together with
// the attempt they were taken for, so a rotation observed on one unit can never
// be presented as another's — the same join gunbc.machine_intake.access
// performs before the delivery solver runs.
//
// previous_credential_epoch is the epoch this unit stood at BEFORE the attempt:
// a rotation that re-writes the same generation is not a rotation.
//
// THE SINGLE published_probe FIELD IS GONE. It answered "did this one host
// reject" and minted BmcSecured while a second LAN address on the same
// controller still accepted. The published-credential readback is now a census
// of every channel the controller reported, plus a probe list joined to that
// census by identity. An empty census is not a one-host observation wearing a
// new name: it refuses rather than adjudicate.
type BmcCredentialRotationObservation sole_constructor {
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint
  previous_credential_epoch: Int
  bootstrap_probe: CredentialProbeOutcome
  rotation: CredentialRotationApplication
  managed_probe: CredentialProbeOutcome
  channel_census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef
  census_observed_at: EpochMs
  published_probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>
  published_user: IpmiUserId
  published_account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation
}

fn observed_bmc_credential_rotation(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  previous_credential_epoch: Int,
  bootstrap_probe: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  rotation: CredentialRotationApplication,
  managed_probe: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  channel_census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census_observed_at: EpochMs,
  published_probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation,
) -> BmcCredentialRotationObservation {
  BmcCredentialRotationObservation {
    subject: subject,
    endpoint: endpoint,
    previous_credential_epoch: previous_credential_epoch,
    bootstrap_probe: bootstrap_probe,
    rotation: rotation,
    managed_probe: managed_probe,
    channel_census: channel_census,
    census_evidence: census_evidence,
    census_observed_at: census_observed_at,
    published_probes: published_probes,
    published_user: published_user,
    published_account: published_account,
  }
}

// EVERY WAY THE STEP REFUSES, each naming which reading failed rather than a
// generic "rotation failed". Two of the three access states the design doc
// names keep their names from that ruling: CredentialStateUnknown and
// PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired. The third is renamed here to
// AccountManagementUnreachable, because AccountManagementUnavailable is already
// the arm of CredentialRotationApplication that says the service did not
// answer, and one spelling for the OBSERVATION and the REFUSAL derived from it
// would be one name for two facts — a fork of exactly the kind DESIGN §3 names,
// inside a single module.
//
// PublishedCredentialStillAccepted is the discriminating refusal this phase
// exists for: everything else about the rotation succeeded and the machine is
// still open on its published default.
//
// PhaseReceiptForAnotherSubject is the state-shaped fold's subject join, minted only by
// bmc_secure_standing_of_phase_receipt: a converged phase receipt is about ONE unit, and a consumer
// that names a different one gets this refusal rather than the standing of the unit the readback
// actually covers. It is deliberately NOT RotationObservationForOtherAttempt under a second reading:
// that arm's label asserts a rotation observation, and a receipt whose conjunction was satisfied
// BEFORE any write (the Noop arm) records that no rotation was applied at all — one name for two
// facts is the fork DESIGN §3 names, and a label that overstates what the carrier holds is §4d.
type BmcSecureRefusalCause
  = RotationObservationForOtherAttempt { expected: MachineIntakeSubject, found: MachineIntakeSubject }
  | CredentialStateUnknown { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired
  | AccountManagementUnreachable { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | CredentialRotationNotApplied
  | CredentialEpochNotAdvanced { previous: Int, observed: Int }
  | ManagedCredentialRejected
  | ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: EpochMs, probed_at: EpochMs }
  | PublishedCredentialStillAccepted { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: EpochMs, probed_at: EpochMs }
  | PublishedCredentialCensusPrecedesRotation { applied_at: EpochMs, observed_at: EpochMs }
  | PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation { applied_at: EpochMs, observed_at: EpochMs }
  | PublishedCredentialCensusNotTaken
  | PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember
  | PublishedCredentialLanMemberUnaddressed { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialChannelAccessNotClosed { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialCensusMemberUnprobed { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialProbeUnmatched { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialRetainedNotAdmittedByProdRiskPolicy
  | PublishedCredentialNotRetained { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PhaseReceiptForAnotherSubject { expected: MachineIntakeSubject, found: MachineIntakeSubject }

// NO ARM RETURNS UnitHardware, AND THAT IS THE POINT (design §6: a non-working
// factory credential is an access state -> PartsHold, not ReturnWindow, absent
// other evidence). gunbc.machine_intake.disposition routes a UnitHardware
// refusal to ReturnWindow, which starts a return clock against the seller; a
// credential the operator has not rotated, an unreachable account service and a
// readback we could not take are not defects of the unit. Because the receipt's
// owner is derived here rather than authored at the call site, no caller can
// file a rotation refusal as a hardware defect.
fn bmc_secure_refusal_owner(cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause) -> QualificationRefusalOwner {
  match cause {
    RotationObservationForOtherAttempt { expected: _, found: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    CredentialStateUnknown { detail: _ } => BmcAccess
    PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired => BmcAccess
    AccountManagementUnreachable { detail: _ } => BmcAccess
    CredentialRotationNotApplied => OperatorAction
    CredentialEpochNotAdvanced { previous: _, observed: _ } => OperatorAction
    ManagedCredentialRejected => OperatorAction
    ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: _ } => BmcAccess
    ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialStillAccepted { channel: _ } => OperatorAction
    PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: _ } => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialCensusPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialCensusNotTaken => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialLanMemberUnaddressed { channel: _ } => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialChannelAccessNotClosed { channel: _ } => OperatorAction
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: _ } => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialCensusMemberUnprobed { channel: _ } => BmcAccess
    PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialProbeUnmatched { channel: _ } => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialRetainedNotAdmittedByProdRiskPolicy => QualificationPolicy
    PublishedCredentialNotRetained { channel: _ } => OperatorAction
    PhaseReceiptForAnotherSubject { expected: _, found: _ } => QualificationPolicy
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_refusal_label(cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match cause {
    RotationObservationForOtherAttempt { expected: _, found: _ } => "rotation observation belongs to another intake attempt"
    CredentialStateUnknown { detail: _ } => "bootstrap credential probe did not establish a credential state"
    PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired => "bootstrap credential no longer authenticates; the previously rotated credential is required"
    AccountManagementUnreachable { detail: _ } => "bmc account management was unreachable"
    CredentialRotationNotApplied => "no credential rotation was applied"
    CredentialEpochNotAdvanced { previous: _, observed: _ } => "credential epoch did not advance past the epoch this unit already stood at"
    ManagedCredentialRejected => "the rotated managed credential does not authenticate"
    ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: _ } => "the rotated managed credential readback did not establish a credential state"
    ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => "the managed credential readback precedes the rotation it claims to verify"
    PublishedCredentialStillAccepted { channel: _ } => "the published factory credential still authenticates after rotation on a census LAN member"
    PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: _ } => "the published factory credential readback did not establish whether it still authenticates"
    PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => "the published credential readback precedes the rotation it claims to verify"
    PublishedCredentialCensusPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => "the channel census was taken before the rotation it claims to verify"
    PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => "the published-account user-list reading precedes the rotation it claims to verify"
    PublishedCredentialCensusNotTaken => "no controller channel census was taken; a single-address probe cannot adjudicate retirement"
    PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember => "the channel census contained no addressable LAN member to probe"
    PublishedCredentialLanMemberUnaddressed { channel: _ } => "a LAN census member has no usable address and the published account still has access on that channel"
    PublishedCredentialChannelAccessNotClosed { channel: _ } => "the published account still has channel access (not NO ACCESS) on a census member"
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: _ } => "Get User Access for the published user was not present on a census member"
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: _ } => "more than one Get User Access row matched the published user on the same census member"
    PublishedCredentialCensusMemberUnprobed { channel: _ } => "a census LAN member has no matching published-credential probe"
    PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: _ } => "more than one published-credential probe matched the same census LAN member"
    PublishedCredentialProbeUnmatched { channel: _ } => "a published-credential probe matched no census LAN member"
    PublishedCredentialRetainedNotAdmittedByProdRiskPolicy => "a retained BMC backdoor is not admitted under a ProdRisk-admitting qualification policy; a fresh census pass that retires or disables the published credential is required"
    PublishedCredentialNotRetained { channel: _ } => "the declared factory-credential retention was not observed on a census LAN member"
    PhaseReceiptForAnotherSubject { expected: _, found: _ } => "the converged phase receipt was read for another intake subject"
  }
}

// The satisfied terminal keeps the reference and the readings it rests on, so a
// later reader can say WHICH rotation secured the unit and WHERE its evidence
// is. The password is not among them, structurally.
//
// published_credential SITS ON BmcSecured, NOT AS A REFUSAL AND NOT AS A
// SECOND SATISFIED COPRODUCT ARM. DisabledNotRetired is a real secured
// outcome: every addressable LAN member rejected the published credential, so
// the phase conjunction holds now. The residual is that a typed restore path
// would bring the account back. A third BmcSecureOutcome arm that also mapped
// to ReceiptSatisfied would be two names for one satisfied standing. A refusal
// would file a currently-closed published login as an unsatisfied phase and
// block fleet admission for a residual that is not an open session. The
// residual travels with the standing; it does not reopen the door.
// latest_admitted_probe_at is the max observed_at among admitted LAN probes,
// including accepted probes on the factory-retention path — not census
// order, and not a claim about when the door closed.
type BmcSecureOutcome
  = BmcSecured {
      endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
      reference: ManagedCredentialReference,
      evidence: List<EvidenceRef>,
      latest_admitted_probe_at: EpochMs,
      published_credential: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation,
    }
  | BmcSecureRefused { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause }

// THE STANDING CARRIES THE SUBJECT AND THE QUALIFICATION POLICY IT WAS
// ADJUDICATED UNDER, AND BOTH JOINS ARE SEALED. An earlier cut returned the
// outcome alone and had bmc_secure_phase_receipt take the subject as a
// separate argument, so a standing legitimately derived for host A could be
// handed to the receipt function beside host B's subject. The same hatch
// existed for policy: derive wrote a TestRisk-admitting policy and the receipt took a
// second ProdRisk-admitting policy, restamping the digest. The receipt now reads
// subject and policy off the standing; there is no parameter left to swap.
// Promotion is a fresh derive_bmc_secure under a ProdRisk-admitting policy, which refuses
// RetainedByPolicy. There is no observed risk class on the unit, and a machine never holds one; the policy
// is the declared qualification (FleetAdmissionReceipt already binds its
// digest). A caller can still declare admits: TestRisk — that is the policy
// fact, not a second knob beside the receipt.
//
// So the subject and the outcome are ONE record and the record is
// sole_constructor: derive_bmc_secure is its only mint, and the receipt
// projection reads the subject off the standing rather than accepting one. A
// cross-attempt replay has no argument left to swap.
//
// THE CEILING, SCOPED RATHER THAN OVERCLAIMED, on this repository's own
// precedent (gunbc.auth.secret_access_admission, and the coproduct-variant form
// falsified at test.claim.inventory_admitted_ledger_seal_livetree_witness):
// sole_constructor seals RECORDS, not coproduct arms, which is why the pairing
// and not the outcome is the sealed carrier — a caller may still write a
// BmcSecured OUTCOME literal, and it reaches nothing, because every consumer
// takes the standing. And the seal is not claimed for the emitted-Rust path,
// where DESIGN records by execution that a sole_constructor type's emitted
// mirror is forgeable; that is a known gap in the mechanism, not a property of
// this carrier.
//
// The seal was taken as a fixture-boundary red once during authoring -- a
// foreign module writing the record literal refuses with
// "sole_constructor type 'BmcSecureStanding' cannot be constructed outside its
// defining module" -- and is not re-enrolled here as a standing gate, because
// the mechanism's general coverage is gunbc.guarantee_probe_corpus
// sole_constructor_cross_module_class and its probes; a per-carrier copy of
// that gate would be the redundant work DESIGN §2 prices. The witness obtains
// every standing FROM derive_bmc_secure, cross-module, so what is confined is
// the construction and not the type's usability.
type BmcSecureStanding sole_constructor {
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject
  policy: MachineQualificationPolicy
  outcome: BmcSecureOutcome
}

fn bmc_secure_evidence(
  bootstrap: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  rotation_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  managed: EvidenceRef,
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  published_probe_evidence: List<EvidenceRef>,
  account_evidence: EvidenceRef,
) -> List<EvidenceRef> {
  let head = match credential_probe_evidence(outcome: bootstrap) {
    Present { value: e } => [e]
    Absent => []
  }
  concat(concat(concat(head, [rotation_evidence, managed, census_evidence]), published_probe_evidence), [account_evidence])
}

fn published_account_evidence(account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation) -> EvidenceRef {
  match account {
    PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: e, observed_at: _ } => e
    PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _, evidence: e, observed_at: _ } => e
    PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy { retention: _, evidence: e, observed_at: _ } => e
  }
}

fn published_account_observed_at(account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation) -> EpochMs {
  match account {
    PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: _, observed_at: at } => at
    PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _, evidence: _, observed_at: at } => at
    PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy { retention: _, evidence: _, observed_at: at } => at
  }
}

fn published_account_requires_published_closed(account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation) -> Bool {
  match account {
    PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: _, observed_at: _ } => true
    PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _, evidence: _, observed_at: _ } => true
    PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy { retention: k, evidence: _, observed_at: _ } =>
      match k {
        BreakGlassAccount { secret: _ } => true
        PublishedFactoryCredential => false
      }
  }
}

// Join identity is (channel, address). Packed as one Int so the census fold looks up
// rather than scanning probes per member (DESIGN §6: a quadratic fold is always fixed).
fn published_lan_identity_key(channel: IpmiChannelNumber, address: Ipv4Address) -> Int {
  ((channel as Int) * 4294967296)
    + ((((address.octet1 as Int) * 16777216) + ((address.octet2 as Int) * 65536))
      + ((address.octet3 as Int) * 256) + (address.octet4 as Int))
}

type PublishedProbeSlot
  = OneProbe { probe: PublishedCredentialLanProbe }
  | SeveralProbes

fn insert_published_probe_slot(
  acc: Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot>,
  p: PublishedCredentialLanProbe,
) -> Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot> {
  let key = published_lan_identity_key(channel: p.channel, address: p.address)
  match map_get(acc, key) {
    Absent => map_insert(acc, key, OneProbe { probe: p })
    Present { value: slot } =>
      match slot {
        OneProbe { probe: _ } => map_insert(acc, key, SeveralProbes)
        SeveralProbes => acc
      }
  }
}

fn index_published_probes(probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>) -> Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot> {
  fold(probes, init: empty_map(), f: (acc, p) => insert_published_probe_slot(acc: acc, p: p))
}

fn bump_assigned_lan_identity(
  acc: Map<Int, Int>,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  address: Ipv4Address,
) -> Map<Int, Int> {
  let key = published_lan_identity_key(channel: channel, address: address)
  match map_get(acc, key) {
    Absent => map_insert(acc, key, 1)
    Present { value: n } => map_insert(acc, key, n + 1)
  }
}

fn index_assigned_lan_identities(members: List<IpmiChannelCensusMember>) -> Map<Int, Int> {
  fold(
    members,
    init: empty_map(),
    f: (acc, m) =>
      match m {
        IpmiNonLanChannelMember { channel: _, medium: _ } => acc
        IpmiLanChannelMember { channel: ch, medium: _, ipv4: cfg } =>
          match cfg {
            IpmiLanIpv4Unassigned => acc
            IpmiLanIpv4Assigned { address: a } => bump_assigned_lan_identity(acc: acc, channel: ch, address: a)
          }
      },
  )
}

type CensusJoinProgress
  = CensusJoinOpen { evidence: List<EvidenceRef>, latest_admitted_probe_at: EpochMs?, saw_addressable_lan: Bool }
  | CensusJoinClosed { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause }

// ONE SOURCE for whether an assigned-LAN probe admits or refuses. A later
// re-match of probe.outcome that closed Accepted/Unestablished independently
// made the RED-1 mutation receipt void (review 65033): changing this function's
// Accepted arm to none still closed in the caller with the same cause.
type PublishedProbeAdjudication
  = PublishedProbeRefused { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause }
  | PublishedProbeAdmitted { evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: EpochMs }

fn adjudicate_published_probe(
  probe: PublishedCredentialLanProbe,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  require_published_closed: Bool,
) -> PublishedProbeAdjudication {
  match probe.outcome {
    CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: d } =>
      PublishedProbeRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: d } }
    CredentialAccepted { evidence: e, observed_at: at } =>
      if require_published_closed {
        PublishedProbeRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialStillAccepted { channel: channel } }
      } else if at < applied_at {
        PublishedProbeRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: applied_at, probed_at: at } }
      } else {
        PublishedProbeAdmitted { evidence: e, observed_at: at }
      }
    CredentialRejected { evidence: e, observed_at: at } =>
      if require_published_closed {
        if at < applied_at {
          PublishedProbeRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: applied_at, probed_at: at } }
        } else {
          PublishedProbeAdmitted { evidence: e, observed_at: at }
        }
      } else {
        PublishedProbeRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialNotRetained { channel: channel } }
      }
  }
}

type LaterAdmittedProbeTime
  = TakePrevious
  | TakeObserved

fn later_admitted_probe_time_choice(prev_i: Int, observed_i: Int) -> LaterAdmittedProbeTime {
  if prev_i < observed_i {
    TakeObserved
  } else {
    TakePrevious
  }
}

fn later_admitted_probe_at(previous: EpochMs?, observed_at: EpochMs) -> EpochMs {
  match previous {
    Absent => observed_at
    Present { value: prev } =>
      match later_admitted_probe_time_choice(prev_i: prev as Int, observed_i: observed_at as Int) {
        TakePrevious => prev
        TakeObserved => observed_at
      }
  }
}

fn join_open_assigned_lan(
  ev: List<EvidenceRef>,
  previous: EpochMs?,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  address: Ipv4Address,
  probe_index: Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot>,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  require_published_closed: Bool,
) -> CensusJoinProgress {
  match map_get(probe_index, published_lan_identity_key(channel: channel, address: address)) {
    Absent => CensusJoinClosed { cause: PublishedCredentialCensusMemberUnprobed { channel: channel } }
    Present { value: slot } =>
      match slot {
        SeveralProbes => CensusJoinClosed { cause: PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: channel } }
        OneProbe { probe: probe } =>
          match adjudicate_published_probe(probe: probe, channel: channel, applied_at: applied_at, require_published_closed: require_published_closed) {
            PublishedProbeRefused { cause: c } => CensusJoinClosed { cause: c }
            PublishedProbeAdmitted { evidence: pe, observed_at: at } =>
              CensusJoinOpen {
                evidence: concat(ev, [pe]),
                latest_admitted_probe_at: Present { value: later_admitted_probe_at(previous: previous, observed_at: at) },
                saw_addressable_lan: true,
              }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn join_assigned_lan_member(
  progress: CensusJoinProgress,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  address: Ipv4Address,
  probe_index: Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot>,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  require_published_closed: Bool,
) -> CensusJoinProgress {
  match progress {
    CensusJoinClosed { cause: c } => CensusJoinClosed { cause: c }
    CensusJoinOpen { evidence: ev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: _ } =>
      join_open_assigned_lan(
        ev: ev,
        previous: latest,
        channel: channel,
        address: address,
        probe_index: probe_index,
        applied_at: applied_at,
        require_published_closed: require_published_closed,
      )
  }
}

fn published_user_access_key(channel: IpmiChannelNumber, user: IpmiUserId) -> Int {
  ((channel as Int) * 64) + (user as Int)
}

type PublishedUserAccessSlot
  = OneUserAccess { access: IpmiUserChannelAccess }
  | SeveralUserAccess

fn insert_published_user_access_slot(
  acc: Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot>,
  row: IpmiUserChannelAccess,
) -> Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot> {
  let key = published_user_access_key(channel: row.channel, user: row.user)
  match map_get(acc, key) {
    Absent => map_insert(acc, key, OneUserAccess { access: row })
    Present { value: slot } =>
      match slot {
        OneUserAccess { access: _ } => map_insert(acc, key, SeveralUserAccess)
        SeveralUserAccess => acc
      }
  }
}

fn index_published_user_access(rows: List<IpmiUserChannelAccess>) -> Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot> {
  fold(rows, init: empty_map(), f: (acc, row) => insert_published_user_access_slot(acc: acc, row: row))
}

fn published_user_privilege_on_channel(
  access_index: Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot>,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
) -> BmcSecureRefusalCause? {
  match map_get(access_index, published_user_access_key(channel: channel, user: published_user)) {
    Absent => Present { value: PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: channel } }
    Present { value: slot } =>
      match slot {
        SeveralUserAccess => Present { value: PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: channel } }
        OneUserAccess { access: row } =>
          if row.privilege == IpmiPrivilegeNoAccess {
            none
          } else {
            Present { value: PublishedCredentialChannelAccessNotClosed { channel: channel } }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn unaddressed_lan_published_access_cause(
  access_index: Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot>,
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
) -> BmcSecureRefusalCause? {
  match map_get(access_index, published_user_access_key(channel: channel, user: published_user)) {
    Absent => Present { value: PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: channel } }
    Present { value: slot } =>
      match slot {
        SeveralUserAccess => Present { value: PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: channel } }
        OneUserAccess { access: row } =>
          if row.privilege == IpmiPrivilegeNoAccess {
            none
          } else {
            Present { value: PublishedCredentialLanMemberUnaddressed { channel: channel } }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn join_census_member(
  progress: CensusJoinProgress,
  member: IpmiChannelCensusMember,
  probe_index: Map<Int, PublishedProbeSlot>,
  access_index: Map<Int, PublishedUserAccessSlot>,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  require_published_closed: Bool,
) -> CensusJoinProgress {
  match progress {
    CensusJoinClosed { cause: c } => CensusJoinClosed { cause: c }
    CensusJoinOpen { evidence: ev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: saw } =>
      match member {
        IpmiNonLanChannelMember { channel: ch, medium: _ } =>
          match published_user_privilege_on_channel(access_index: access_index, channel: ch, published_user: published_user) {
            Present { value: c } => CensusJoinClosed { cause: c }
            Absent => CensusJoinOpen { evidence: ev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: saw }
          }
        IpmiLanChannelMember { channel: ch, medium: _, ipv4: cfg } =>
          match cfg {
            IpmiLanIpv4Unassigned =>
              match unaddressed_lan_published_access_cause(access_index: access_index, channel: ch, published_user: published_user) {
                Present { value: c } => CensusJoinClosed { cause: c }
                Absent => CensusJoinOpen { evidence: ev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: saw }
              }
            IpmiLanIpv4Assigned { address: a } =>
              join_assigned_lan_member(
                progress: CensusJoinOpen { evidence: ev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: true },
                channel: ch,
                address: a,
                probe_index: probe_index,
                applied_at: applied_at,
                require_published_closed: require_published_closed,
              )
          }
      }
  }
}

fn probe_unmatched_or_duplicate(
  probe: PublishedCredentialLanProbe,
  assigned_index: Map<Int, Int>,
) -> BmcSecureRefusalCause? {
  match map_get(assigned_index, published_lan_identity_key(channel: probe.channel, address: probe.address)) {
    Absent => Present { value: PublishedCredentialProbeUnmatched { channel: probe.channel } }
    Present { value: n } =>
      if n > 1 {
        Present { value: PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: probe.channel } }
      } else {
        none
      }
  }
}

fn unmatched_published_probe_cause(
  probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>,
  assigned_index: Map<Int, Int>,
) -> BmcSecureRefusalCause? {
  fold(
    probes,
    init: none,
    f: (acc, p) =>
      match acc {
        Present { value: c } => Present { value: c }
        Absent => probe_unmatched_or_duplicate(probe: p, assigned_index: assigned_index)
      },
  )
}

// THE PUBLISHED-CREDENTIAL READBACK IS A FOLD OVER THE CONTROLLER CHANNEL
// CENSUS. Assigned LAN members still require an identity-joined login probe.
// Unaddressed LAN (0.0.0.0) and non-LAN members join on Get User Access for
// observation.published_user: NO ACCESS closes the member; any other privilege
// refuses; a missing or duplicated (channel, user) row refuses. A NO ACCESS
// row for a different user does not close this one (review 65645).
// That is the unit-1 fact: channel 7 is 802.3 with a permanent unspecified
// address, and the rotation set admin to NO ACCESS on ch2, ch7 and ch8.
// Treating unaddressed as unconditionally open would refuse that controller
// forever (DESIGN §4d over-prohibition). An unaddressed channel that still
// holds ADMINISTRATOR is the exposure the moment it gets an address.
// A census taken before rotation is not the universe that join is complete
// against: a channel the rotation enabled would be absent from the roster.
// adjudicate_published_census_join refuses CensusPrecedesRotation once, before
// the fold, so assigned-LAN members cannot skip the ordering the unaddressed
// and non-LAN arms used to carry twice.
//
// RUNG: mechanically preventable. Ceiling is enrolled one-arm mutants on the
// merge path (DESIGN §4b(4)): a deletion of a guarding arm that reddens exactly
// the named witness. Next-rung trigger: that mutation capability for
// test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_witness on required CI, not a
// scratch-tree one-shot. Named-cause witnesses in that module are the enrolled
// evidence this PR keeps executing. Do not cite an un-enrolled local run.
fn adjudicate_published_census_join(
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  reference: ManagedCredentialReference,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  rotation_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  bootstrap: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  managed_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census_observed_at: EpochMs,
  probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  if list_length(items: census.members) == 0 {
    BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialCensusNotTaken }
  } else if census_observed_at < applied_at {
    BmcSecureRefused {
      cause: PublishedCredentialCensusPrecedesRotation { applied_at: applied_at, observed_at: census_observed_at },
    }
  } else {
    let require_closed = published_account_requires_published_closed(account: published_account)
    let probe_index = index_published_probes(probes: probes)
    let assigned_index = index_assigned_lan_identities(members: census.members)
    let access_index = index_published_user_access(rows: census.user_access)
    let joined = fold(
      census.members,
      init: CensusJoinOpen { evidence: [], latest_admitted_probe_at: none, saw_addressable_lan: false },
      f: (acc, m) => join_census_member(
        progress: acc,
        member: m,
        probe_index: probe_index,
        access_index: access_index,
        published_user: published_user,
        applied_at: applied_at,
        require_published_closed: require_closed,
      ),
    )
    match joined {
      CensusJoinClosed { cause: c } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: c }
      CensusJoinOpen { evidence: pev, latest_admitted_probe_at: latest, saw_addressable_lan: saw } =>
        if saw == false {
          BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember }
        } else {
          match unmatched_published_probe_cause(probes: probes, assigned_index: assigned_index) {
            Present { value: c } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: c }
            Absent =>
              match latest {
                Absent => BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember }
                Present { value: at } =>
                  BmcSecured {
                    endpoint: endpoint,
                    reference: reference,
                    evidence: bmc_secure_evidence(
                      bootstrap: bootstrap,
                      rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
                      managed: managed_evidence,
                      census_evidence: census_evidence,
                      published_probe_evidence: pev,
                      account_evidence: published_account_evidence(account: published_account),
                    ),
                    latest_admitted_probe_at: at,
                    published_credential: published_account,
                  }
              }
          }
        }
    }
  }
}

fn adjudicate_published_census(
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  reference: ManagedCredentialReference,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  rotation_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  bootstrap: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  managed_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census_observed_at: EpochMs,
  probes: List<PublishedCredentialLanProbe>,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_account: PublishedCredentialAccountObservation,
  admits: DeploymentRiskClass,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  let account_at = published_account_observed_at(account: published_account)
  if account_at < applied_at {
    BmcSecureRefused {
      cause: PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation { applied_at: applied_at, observed_at: account_at },
    }
  } else {
    match published_account {
    PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy { retention: _, evidence: _, observed_at: _ } =>
      match admits {
        ProdRisk => BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialRetainedNotAdmittedByProdRiskPolicy }
        TestRisk =>
          adjudicate_published_census_join(
            endpoint: endpoint,
            reference: reference,
            applied_at: applied_at,
            rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
            bootstrap: bootstrap,
            managed_evidence: managed_evidence,
            census: census,
            census_evidence: census_evidence,
            census_observed_at: census_observed_at,
            probes: probes,
            published_user: published_user,
            published_account: published_account,
          )
      }
    PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: _, observed_at: _ } =>
      adjudicate_published_census_join(
        endpoint: endpoint,
        reference: reference,
        applied_at: applied_at,
        rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
        bootstrap: bootstrap,
        managed_evidence: managed_evidence,
        census: census,
        census_evidence: census_evidence,
        census_observed_at: census_observed_at,
        probes: probes,
        published_user: published_user,
        published_account: published_account,
      )
    PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _, evidence: _, observed_at: _ } =>
      adjudicate_published_census_join(
        endpoint: endpoint,
        reference: reference,
        applied_at: applied_at,
        rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
        bootstrap: bootstrap,
        managed_evidence: managed_evidence,
        census: census,
        census_evidence: census_evidence,
        census_observed_at: census_observed_at,
        probes: probes,
        published_user: published_user,
        published_account: published_account,
      )
  }
  }
}

// The managed credential must work, and must have been read after the rotation
// that created it. A pre-rotation acceptance would be a reading of whatever
// account already answered to that name.
fn adjudicate_managed_probe(
  observation: BmcCredentialRotationObservation,
  reference: ManagedCredentialReference,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  rotation_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  managed: CredentialProbeOutcome,
  admits: DeploymentRiskClass,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  match managed {
    CredentialRejected { evidence: _, observed_at: _ } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialRejected }
    CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: d } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: d } }
    CredentialAccepted { evidence: me, observed_at: at } =>
      if at < applied_at {
        BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: applied_at, probed_at: at } }
      } else {
        adjudicate_published_census(
          endpoint: observation.endpoint,
          reference: reference,
          applied_at: applied_at,
          rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
          bootstrap: observation.bootstrap_probe,
          managed_evidence: me,
          census: observation.channel_census,
          census_evidence: observation.census_evidence,
          census_observed_at: observation.census_observed_at,
          probes: observation.published_probes,
          published_user: observation.published_user,
          published_account: observation.published_account,
          admits: admits,
        )
      }
  }
}

fn adjudicate_rotation(
  observation: BmcCredentialRotationObservation,
  reference: ManagedCredentialReference,
  applied_at: EpochMs,
  rotation_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  admits: DeploymentRiskClass,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  if (reference.credential_epoch <= observation.previous_credential_epoch) {
    BmcSecureRefused {
      cause: CredentialEpochNotAdvanced {
        previous: observation.previous_credential_epoch,
        observed: reference.credential_epoch,
      },
    }
  } else {
    adjudicate_managed_probe(
      observation: observation,
      reference: reference,
      applied_at: applied_at,
      rotation_evidence: rotation_evidence,
      managed: observation.managed_probe,
      admits: admits,
    )
  }
}

fn adjudicate_bootstrap(
  observation: BmcCredentialRotationObservation,
  admits: DeploymentRiskClass,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  match observation.bootstrap_probe {
    CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: d } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: CredentialStateUnknown { detail: d } }
    CredentialRejected { evidence: _, observed_at: _ } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired }
    CredentialAccepted { evidence: _, observed_at: _ } =>
      match observation.rotation {
        RotationNotAttempted => BmcSecureRefused { cause: CredentialRotationNotApplied }
        AccountManagementUnavailable { detail: d } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: AccountManagementUnreachable { detail: d } }
        RotationApplied { reference: r, applied_at: at, evidence: e } =>
          adjudicate_rotation(
            observation: observation,
            reference: r,
            applied_at: at,
            rotation_evidence: e,
            admits: admits,
          )
      }
  }
}

fn derive_bmc_secure(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  observation: BmcCredentialRotationObservation,
  policy: MachineQualificationPolicy,
) -> BmcSecureStanding {
  let outcome = if same_intake_subject(left: subject, right: observation.subject) == false {
    BmcSecureRefused { cause: RotationObservationForOtherAttempt { expected: subject, found: observation.subject } }
  } else {
    adjudicate_bootstrap(observation: observation, admits: policy.admits)
  }
  BmcSecureStanding { subject: subject, policy: policy, outcome: outcome }
}

data bmc_secure_phase: IntakePhase = Arrival { phase: BmcSecure }

fn bmc_secure_receipt_result(standing: BmcSecureStanding) -> IntakeReceiptResult {
  match standing.outcome {
    BmcSecured { endpoint: _, reference: _, evidence: _, latest_admitted_probe_at: _, published_credential: _ } => ReceiptSatisfied
    BmcSecureRefused { cause: c } =>
      ReceiptRefused { owner: bmc_secure_refusal_owner(cause: c), cause: bmc_secure_refusal_label(cause: c) }
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_receipt_observations(standing: BmcSecureStanding) -> List<EvidenceRef> {
  match standing.outcome {
    BmcSecured { endpoint: _, reference: _, evidence: e, latest_admitted_probe_at: _, published_credential: _ } => e
    BmcSecureRefused { cause: _ } => []
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_phase_receipt(
  standing: BmcSecureStanding,
  producer: IntakeProducerIdentity,
  started_at: EpochMs,
  ended_at: EpochMs,
  previous_receipt: ContentHash?,
) -> IntakeReceiptEnvelope {
  IntakeReceiptEnvelope {
    schema: MachineIntakeReceiptV1,
    subject: standing.subject,
    phase: bmc_secure_phase,
    producer: producer,
    policy_digest: machine_qualification_policy_digest(policy: standing.policy),
    started_at: started_at,
    ended_at: ended_at,
    observations: bmc_secure_receipt_observations(standing: standing),
    result: bmc_secure_receipt_result(standing: standing),
    previous_receipt: previous_receipt,
  }
}

// ══ BmcSecure AS A DESIRED STATE (docs/plans/managed-host-untangle.md, cut O1b) ══════════════════
//
// THE DEFECT THIS SECTION REPAIRS. derive_bmc_secure above is rotation-EVENT shaped: a rejected
// bootstrap credential refuses PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired, an accepted one with no rotation
// refuses CredentialRotationNotApplied, and only RotationApplied with an advanced epoch can mint
// BmcSecured. So a correctly secured controller -- managed credential accepted, published credential
// refused on every LAN member of the channel census -- cannot be observed as already secured. The
// phase is decomposed here instead: observe the CURRENT account state (independent of whether this
// invocation rotated anything), Noop only when the existing conjunction already holds, otherwise
// Apply a typed account action over an admitted route, then re-read independently and derive the
// standing from that readback alone.
//
// THE CONJUNCTION AND THE CENSUS JOIN ARE NOT RESTATED. adjudicate_published_census above is the one
// authority for the published half; this section calls it with the observation's read floor where
// the event path passed applied_at, projecting observer instants to their millis only at that call.
// The managed half (accepted, read at or after the floor) is the same test adjudicate_managed_probe
// makes, over the observer clock.
//
// SHADOW, NOT YET THE AUTHORITY (operator ruling C, eager-gull-22, 2026-10-04). The event path above
// stays as the standing mtcollins1 and managed_hosts() read, FROZEN: no new consumer may use it. Its
// deletion and mtcollins1's re-expression in this shape are one held transition, made together with a
// committed read-only post-reflash probe and the operator-approved wet Apply on that unit
// (bmc_secure_state_cutover_frontier). Until then the executing consumers of this section are its dry
// realization over gunbc.bmc_model BmcWorld and that realization's witness.
//
// PER CONTROLLER FAMILY (ruling gunbc.design_ruling bmc_secure_goes_live_per_controller_family, 2026-10-28).
// The operator admitted this section as the live authority for the ASRock ALTRAD8UD / OpenBMC family ahead
// of the held transition, the event path staying frozen for mtcollins1 alone. That family's published
// account is the managed account (root), which is the PublishedCredentialRetiredOnTheManagedAccount reading
// below; its live read and apply are the two frontiers at the end of this module.

// A CONTROLLER'S OWN CLOCK IS AN OBSERVATION OF THE CONTROLLER, NEVER AN ORDERING CLOCK. mtjade1's BMC
// reports the year 2000. The reading is kept, with its evidence, and it is not an ordering clock: every
// ordering field below is gunbc.clock_read ObserverClockInstant, which only the observer mints, and the
// sealed mints refuse this type at their call arguments. Not wider: a non-literal value of this type
// in a record field typed ObserverClockInstant is accepted today
// (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode record_field_admits_a_distinct_product_value).
type ControllerClockReading {
  reported_millis: EpochMs
  evidence: EvidenceRef
}

// ONE AUTHENTICATION ATTEMPT, TIMED BY THE OBSERVER. The three arms of CredentialProbeOutcome with an
// observer instant where it carries a bare EpochMs; the event path's type dies with the event path.
//
// EVERY ORDERING FIELD SITS IN A SEALED RECORD WHOSE MINT TAKES THE INSTANT AS A PARAMETER. A field
// typed ObserverClockInstant does not by itself keep another product out of it: a non-literal value
// of a distinct product placed in a record or variant field is accepted today
// (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode record_field_admits_a_distinct_product_value), while the same value at
// a call argument refuses. sole_constructor seals records, not coproduct arms, so the probe arms carry
// ObservedReading rather than an instant: a literal outside this module refuses SoleConstructorViolation,
// and the one mint, observed_reading, refuses a ControllerClockReading at its observed_at argument.
type ObservedReading sole_constructor {
  evidence: EvidenceRef
  observed_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

fn observed_reading(evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: ObserverClockInstant) -> ObservedReading
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "dry_probe"),
  ]
{
  ObservedReading { evidence: evidence, observed_at: observed_at }
}

type ObservedCredentialProbe
  = ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: ObservedReading }
  | ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: ObservedReading }
  | ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: NonEmptyStr }

type ObservedPublishedLanProbe {
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber
  address: Ipv4Address
  probe: ObservedCredentialProbe
}

// HOW THE PUBLISHED CREDENTIAL'S STATE WAS ESTABLISHED, and so what it cost.
//
// Probed: the published credential was tried on every addressed LAN member of the channel census, one
// failed login each against the published account's lockout budget. That is the only reading for a
// controller whose published account is a DIFFERENT account from the managed one (mtcollins1: user 2
// beside managed user 3), because nothing else says what that account accepts.
//
// RetiredOnTheManagedAccount: the published login names the very account the managed credential
// authenticates as (OpenBMC root), and the build's credential policy grounds ONE password per account on
// every surface this controller serves (gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_credential_policy). The managed
// generation being accepted on that account then says the published password is not its password on any
// of those surfaces -- derived, with no failed login, so the managed account's own lockout budget is not
// spent proving it. A surface the policy does not ground refuses the derivation; it is never assumed.
type PublishedCredentialEvidence
  = PublishedCredentialProbed { probes: List<ObservedPublishedLanProbe> }
  | PublishedCredentialRetiredOnTheManagedAccount { derivation: SharedStoreRetirement }

type SharedStoreRetirement sole_constructor {
  policy: BmcCredentialPolicyKey
  account: NonEmptyStr
  surfaces: List<SharedCredentialSurface>
}

type SharedStoreRetirementRefusal
  = RetirementAccountIsNotTheManagedAccount { published: NonEmptyStr, managed: NonEmptyStr }
  | RetirementSurfaceNotGroundedAsShared { surface: CredentialSurface, policy: BmcCredentialPolicyKey }
  | RetirementGenerationIsThePublishedPassword
  | RetirementBuildHasNoPolicy { policy: BmcCredentialPolicyKey }
  | RetirementServedSurfacesUnknown

type SharedStoreRetirementOutcome
  = SharedStoreRetirementDerived { derivation: SharedStoreRetirement }
  | SharedStoreRetirementRefused { cause: SharedStoreRetirementRefusal }

fn shared_surface_listed(surfaces: List<SharedCredentialSurface>, surface: CredentialSurface) -> Bool {
  any(surfaces, x => x.surface == surface)
}

// THE DERIVATION'S ONE MINT, run by a reader that holds the generation's bytes: it alone can say whether
// the generation equals the published password (a rotation to the factory password retires nothing).
// `served` is every surface the read found the controller serving.
fn derive_shared_store_retirement(
  policy: BmcCredentialPolicyKey,
  published_account: NonEmptyStr,
  managed_account: NonEmptyStr,
  served: List<CredentialSurface>,
  generation_is_published_password: Bool,
) -> SharedStoreRetirementOutcome
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "dry_published_credential"),
  ]
{
  let shared = shared_store_surfaces(key: policy)
  let unshared: List<CredentialSurface> = filter(served, x => !shared_surface_listed(surfaces: shared, surface: x))
  if (published_account as String) != (managed_account as String) {
    SharedStoreRetirementRefused { cause: RetirementAccountIsNotTheManagedAccount { published: published_account, managed: managed_account } }
  } else if (match bmc_credential_policy_for(key: policy) { Absent => true  Present { value: _ } => false }) {
    SharedStoreRetirementRefused { cause: RetirementBuildHasNoPolicy { policy: policy } }
  } else if list_length(items: served) == 0 {
    SharedStoreRetirementRefused { cause: RetirementServedSurfacesUnknown }
  } else if generation_is_published_password {
    SharedStoreRetirementRefused { cause: RetirementGenerationIsThePublishedPassword }
  } else {
    match list_head(xs: unshared) {
      Absent => SharedStoreRetirementDerived { derivation: SharedStoreRetirement { policy: policy, account: published_account, surfaces: shared } }
      Present { value: first } => SharedStoreRetirementRefused { cause: RetirementSurfaceNotGroundedAsShared { surface: first, policy: policy } }
    }
  }
}

type PublishedAccountKind
  = PublishedAccountRetired
  | PublishedAccountDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: PublishedCredentialRestorePath }
  | PublishedAccountRetainedByPolicy { retention: RetainedCredentialKind }

type ObservedPublishedAccount sole_constructor {
  kind: PublishedAccountKind
  evidence: EvidenceRef
  observed_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

fn observed_published_account(kind: PublishedAccountKind, evidence: EvidenceRef, observed_at: ObserverClockInstant) -> ObservedPublishedAccount
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "dry_read_bmc_account_state"),
  ]
{
  ObservedPublishedAccount { kind: kind, evidence: evidence, observed_at: observed_at }
}

// THE CURRENT ACCOUNT STATE OF ONE CONTROLLER, AS READ. It carries no rotation and no bootstrap probe:
// it is the same reading whether or not anything was written. read_floor is the observer instant the
// read began; every reading in it must be at or after the floor, which is what lets the receipt below
// order a readback after the write it verifies and refuse the pre-write reading passed twice.
// firmware is the release the controller reported in the same read. It is the build a route must be
// grounded for: the plan reads it from here and takes no build argument, so a current reading cannot be
// admitted over a route for a build the controller no longer runs (O1a's stale-route crossing).
// board is the controller's declared board (gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_write_controller row), Absent where no
// row declares one. With firmware it is the credential-policy key (gunbc.machine_intake
// bmc_credential_policy BmcCredentialPolicyKey) a derived retirement must have been grounded by: the key is
// read from here, never supplied beside the reading, and an undeclared board grounds no derivation.
type BmcAccountStateObservation sole_constructor {
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint
  board: BoardAuthorityRef?
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity
  managed: ManagedCredentialReference
  managed_user: IpmiUserId
  attempt: AttemptIdentity
  read_floor: ObserverClockInstant
  managed_probe: ObservedCredentialProbe
  channel_census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef
  census_observed_at: ObserverClockInstant
  published_credential: PublishedCredentialEvidence
  published_user: IpmiUserId
  published_account: ObservedPublishedAccount
  break_glass: ManagedCredentialReference
  break_glass_probe: ObservedCredentialProbe
  controller_clock: ControllerClockReading?
  // THE SERVED LOCKOUT READING, taken beside the other readings of this pass: what
  // this controller serves for AccountService lockout and for the per-channel IPMI
  // LAN Bad Password Threshold, or the typed reason neither could be read. It is a
  // REQUIRED field and not an optional one, because "this plan may not spend a
  // failed login until we know" is the answer, and an optional field would let a
  // caller mean that by forgetting to fill it in. See the section at the end of
  // this module.
  //
  // WHY ITS INSTANT IS PART OF ITS IDENTITY, unlike the controller clock above
  // (which is zeroed before the join): the served threshold is OPERATOR-WRITABLE —
  // an AccountService PATCH, a Set LAN Configuration Parameters — so a reading from
  // an earlier instant may describe a policy the controller no longer has, and two
  // readings that differ only in when they were taken are NOT the same reading here.
  // The consequence is deliberate and costs a pass: a phase that already holds the
  // conjunction but bring a lockout reading from another instant is asked to re-read.
  lockout: BmcControllerLockoutReading
}

fn observed_bmc_account_state(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  board: BoardAuthorityRef?,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  managed: ManagedCredentialReference,
  managed_user: IpmiUserId,
  attempt: AttemptIdentity,
  read_floor: ObserverClockInstant,
  managed_probe: ObservedCredentialProbe,
  channel_census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  census_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  census_observed_at: ObserverClockInstant,
  published_credential: PublishedCredentialEvidence,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_account: ObservedPublishedAccount,
  break_glass: ManagedCredentialReference,
  break_glass_probe: ObservedCredentialProbe,
  controller_clock: ControllerClockReading?,
  lockout: BmcControllerLockoutReading,
) -> BmcAccountStateObservation
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "dry_read_bmc_account_state"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "observation_with_controller_clock"),
  ]
{
  BmcAccountStateObservation {
    subject: subject,
    endpoint: endpoint,
    board: board,
    firmware: firmware,
    managed: managed,
    managed_user: managed_user,
    attempt: attempt,
    read_floor: read_floor,
    managed_probe: managed_probe,
    channel_census: channel_census,
    census_evidence: census_evidence,
    census_observed_at: census_observed_at,
    published_credential: published_credential,
    published_user: published_user,
    published_account: published_account,
    break_glass: break_glass,
    break_glass_probe: break_glass_probe,
    controller_clock: controller_clock,
    lockout: lockout,
  }
}

fn observed_probe_at_join(probe: ObservedCredentialProbe) -> CredentialProbeOutcome {
  match probe {
    ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: r } => CredentialAccepted { evidence: r.evidence, observed_at: observer_instant_millis(instant: r.observed_at) }
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: r } => CredentialRejected { evidence: r.evidence, observed_at: observer_instant_millis(instant: r.observed_at) }
    ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: d } => CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: d }
  }
}

fn observed_published_account_at_join(account: ObservedPublishedAccount) -> PublishedCredentialAccountObservation {
  let at = observer_instant_millis(instant: account.observed_at)
  match account.kind {
    PublishedAccountRetired => PublishedCredentialRetired { evidence: account.evidence, observed_at: at }
    PublishedAccountDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: r } =>
      PublishedCredentialDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: r, evidence: account.evidence, observed_at: at }
    PublishedAccountRetainedByPolicy { retention: k } =>
      PublishedCredentialRetainedByPolicy { retention: k, evidence: account.evidence, observed_at: at }
  }
}

fn observation_with_controller_clock(base: BmcAccountStateObservation, controller_clock: ControllerClockReading?) -> BmcAccountStateObservation
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "bmc_account_state_observation_same"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "apply_with_diverged_controller_clock"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "w_bmc_secure_apply_of_a_different_present_controller_clock_is_refused"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "w_bmc_secure_apply_of_a_present_controller_clock_over_absent_is_refused"),
  ]
{
  observed_bmc_account_state(
    subject: base.subject,
    endpoint: base.endpoint,
    board: base.board,
    firmware: base.firmware,
    managed: base.managed,
    managed_user: base.managed_user,
    attempt: base.attempt,
    read_floor: base.read_floor,
    managed_probe: base.managed_probe,
    channel_census: base.channel_census,
    census_evidence: base.census_evidence,
    census_observed_at: base.census_observed_at,
    published_credential: base.published_credential,
    published_user: base.published_user,
    published_account: base.published_account,
    break_glass: base.break_glass,
    break_glass_probe: base.break_glass_probe,
    controller_clock: controller_clock,
    lockout: base.lockout,
  )
}

fn managed_reference_same(a: ManagedCredentialReference, b: ManagedCredentialReference) -> Bool {
  a.account == b.account
    && a.role == b.role
    && (a.secret.project as String) == (b.secret.project as String)
    && a.secret.secret == b.secret.secret
    && a.secret.version == b.secret.version
    && a.credential_epoch == b.credential_epoch
}

// THE OBSERVATION IS THE PAYLOAD, NOT A START TIME. Record `==` is the language's structural
// relation on the closed type, except controller_clock: ControllerClockReading? inherits
// optional_equality_answers_by_representation, so that field is matched explicitly and the rest
// compared by `==` after zeroing it. That match and observation_with_controller_clock are still
// authored field lists: a new ControllerClockReading field or a new Optional on the observation
// is not derived from the type declaration (no .dag value-layer reader of declared fields). The
// class is gunbc.guarantee_stall.authored_record_field_list_standing_for_type_population_stall
// authored_record_field_list_standing_for_type_population_stall -- a stall below ceiling, not a
// section 4b(3) drop.
fn controller_clock_reading_same(left: ControllerClockReading?, right: ControllerClockReading?) -> Bool {
  match left {
    Absent => match right { Absent => true  Present { value: _ } => false }
    Present { value: a } => match right {
      Absent => false
      Present { value: b } =>
        (a.reported_millis as Int) == (b.reported_millis as Int)
          && a.evidence.label == b.evidence.label
          && content_hash_equal(left: a.evidence.digest, right: b.evidence.digest)
    }
  }
}

fn bmc_account_state_observation_same(a: BmcAccountStateObservation, b: BmcAccountStateObservation) -> Bool {
  controller_clock_reading_same(left: a.controller_clock, right: b.controller_clock)
    && (observation_with_controller_clock(base: a, controller_clock: none)
      == observation_with_controller_clock(base: b, controller_clock: none))
}

// WHAT THE PHASE REQUIRES OF THE CONTROLLER: this managed generation accepted, the published
// credential closed, under this qualification policy.
// published_break_glass is the exact generation the published account is retired TO (or, under a
// break-glass retention policy, the account that must be the one retained): a predeclared secret,
// version and epoch. It is part of the goal so the replacement is a desired state and never whatever
// generation a caller hands the planner. Disabling or deleting the published account instead is not an
// arm here: those are channel and user-table writes no executed evidence grounds on any controller.
type BmcSecureGoal {
  managed: ManagedCredentialReference
  published_break_glass: ManagedCredentialReference
  policy: MachineQualificationPolicy
}

// WHAT AN ASSESSMENT FOUND. The conjunction's own causes, plus the published account's replacement:
// the published user must authenticate with the goal's exact break-glass generation (break_glass /
// break_glass_probe on the reading), observed at or after the read floor. Without it, "factory rejected
// beside an arbitrary replacement" would read as secured, and an Apply could mint a receipt without the
// goal generation ever authenticating. Disable or delete of the published account is not an admitted
// goal arm here; it would carry its own observation, not ride on this probe.
type BmcSecureStateFinding
  = ConjunctionFinding { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause }
  | BreakGlassGenerationRejected
  | BreakGlassGenerationUnestablished { detail: NonEmptyStr }

fn bmc_secure_state_finding_label(finding: BmcSecureStateFinding) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match finding {
    ConjunctionFinding { cause: c } => bmc_secure_refusal_label(cause: c)
    BreakGlassGenerationRejected => "the published account does not authenticate with the goal's break-glass generation"
    BreakGlassGenerationUnestablished { detail: _ } => "the probe of the goal's break-glass generation did not establish a credential state"
  }
}

// The satisfied evidence: the conjunction's BmcSecured, kept with the observation it was read from.
type BmcSecureHeld {
  observation: BmcAccountStateObservation
  evidence: List<EvidenceRef>
}

type BmcSecureStateRefusal
  = AccountStateForOtherSubject { expected: MachineIntakeSubject, found: MachineIntakeSubject }
  | AccountStateForOtherManagedReference { goal: ManagedCredentialReference, observed: ManagedCredentialReference }
  | AccountReadingPrecedesReadFloor { floor: ObserverClockInstant }
  | AccountStateConjunctionRefused { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause }
  | AccountDeviationNeedsUngroundedOperation { cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause, operation: MissingAccountOperation }
  | AccountRetentionNotGoalBound { retained: SecretRef, goal: ManagedCredentialReference }
  | AccountStateForOtherBreakGlassReference { goal: ManagedCredentialReference, observed: ManagedCredentialReference }

// WHICH CONJUNCTION REFUSALS AN ACCOUNT WRITE CAN REMEDY, WHICH ARE UNKNOWNS, AND WHICH ARE NEITHER.
// A deviation is a state the account action changes (the managed credential not accepted, the
// published one still accepted or still holding channel access). An unknown is a reading that did not
// establish a state; it is never a deviation, because writing on an unread controller is the
// absorbing fallback DESIGN §5 forbids. Everything else -- an ordering, a duplicated or unmatched
// reading, a retention under a ProdRisk-admitting policy -- refuses the assessment.
// TWO ADMITTED ACTIONS: a password write (IpmiSetUserPassword) and, since cut O1a-2, a channel-access
// write (the privilege-limit-only Set User Access, IpmiSetUserPrivilegeLimit). A published account still
// holding access on a LAN channel -- addressed or not -- is therefore a DEVIATION the plan remedies, and
// it is admissible ONLY over a GROUNDED channel-access route: the plan mint computes each channel write's
// admission with admit_rotation_apply and refuses on every other arm, so "no admitted route performs a
// channel-access write" is now a typed plan refusal rather than an assessment refusal. Putting the
// factory password back is still not an admitted action, so that deviation still refuses with the
// missing operation named.
type MissingAccountOperation = | PublishedFactoryCredentialRestore

type ConjunctionCauseClass
  = CauseRemediableByAccountAction
  | CauseNeedsUngroundedOperation { operation: MissingAccountOperation }
  | CauseUnestablishedReading
  | CauseReadingPrecedesFloor
  | CauseRefusesAssessment

fn conjunction_cause_class(cause: BmcSecureRefusalCause) -> ConjunctionCauseClass {
  match cause {
    RotationObservationForOtherAttempt { expected: _, found: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
    CredentialStateUnknown { detail: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PreviouslyRotatedCredentialRequired => CauseRefusesAssessment
    AccountManagementUnreachable { detail: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    CredentialRotationNotApplied => CauseRefusesAssessment
    CredentialEpochNotAdvanced { previous: _, observed: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
    ManagedCredentialRejected => CauseRemediableByAccountAction
    ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => CauseReadingPrecedesFloor
    PublishedCredentialStillAccepted { channel: _ } => CauseRemediableByAccountAction
    PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PublishedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, probed_at: _ } => CauseReadingPrecedesFloor
    PublishedCredentialCensusPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => CauseReadingPrecedesFloor
    PublishedCredentialAccountPrecedesRotation { applied_at: _, observed_at: _ } => CauseReadingPrecedesFloor
    PublishedCredentialCensusNotTaken => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PublishedCredentialNoAddressableLanMember => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PublishedCredentialLanMemberUnaddressed { channel: _ } => CauseRemediableByAccountAction
    PublishedCredentialChannelAccessNotClosed { channel: _ } => CauseRemediableByAccountAction
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessUnestablished { channel: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PublishedCredentialUserAccessDuplicate { channel: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
    PublishedCredentialCensusMemberUnprobed { channel: _ } => CauseUnestablishedReading
    PublishedCredentialProbeDuplicate { channel: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
    PublishedCredentialProbeUnmatched { channel: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
    PublishedCredentialRetainedNotAdmittedByProdRiskPolicy => CauseRefusesAssessment
    PublishedCredentialNotRetained { channel: _ } => CauseNeedsUngroundedOperation { operation: PublishedFactoryCredentialRestore }
    // Not minted by the conjunction: this cause belongs to the standing projection beside this fold, and
    // an assessment never sees it. Named so the match stays the forcing function DESIGN §4b wants — a
    // cause added to the coproduct must be classified here before anything compiles.
    PhaseReceiptForAnotherSubject { expected: _, found: _ } => CauseRefusesAssessment
  }
}

fn conjunction_over_observation(goal: BmcSecureGoal, observed: BmcAccountStateObservation) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  let floor = observer_instant_millis(instant: observed.read_floor)
  match observed.managed_probe {
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: _ } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialRejected }
    ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: d } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialUnestablished { detail: d } }
    ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: mr } => {
      let me = mr.evidence
      let at = mr.observed_at
      if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: at, later: observed.read_floor) {
        BmcSecureRefused { cause: ManagedCredentialProbePrecedesRotation { applied_at: floor, probed_at: observer_instant_millis(instant: at) } }
      } else {
        match observed.published_credential {
          PublishedCredentialProbed { probes: probes } =>
            adjudicate_published_census(
              endpoint: observed.endpoint,
              reference: observed.managed,
              applied_at: floor,
              rotation_evidence: me,
              bootstrap: CredentialProbeUnestablished { detail: "no bootstrap probe: the desired-state reading carries none" as NonEmptyStr },
              managed_evidence: me,
              census: observed.channel_census,
              census_evidence: observed.census_evidence,
              census_observed_at: observer_instant_millis(instant: observed.census_observed_at),
              probes: map(probes, p => PublishedCredentialLanProbe { channel: p.channel, address: p.address, outcome: observed_probe_at_join(probe: p.probe) }),
              published_user: observed.published_user,
              published_account: observed_published_account_at_join(account: observed.published_account),
              admits: goal.policy.admits,
            )
          PublishedCredentialRetiredOnTheManagedAccount { derivation: d } =>
            retired_on_the_managed_account(observed: observed, derivation: d, managed_evidence: me, managed_at: at)
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

// THE PUBLISHED HALF WHEN THE PUBLISHED ACCOUNT IS THE MANAGED ONE. There is no published account left to
// close on a channel -- it is the account the managed credential authenticates as, which must keep its
// access -- so the census join over the published user does not apply, and the derivation stands where
// the probes would. The reading must say the account was retired (its password changed), on the same
// IPMI user the managed probe authenticated; anything else is a reading the derivation does not cover.
fn retired_on_the_managed_account(
  observed: BmcAccountStateObservation,
  derivation: SharedStoreRetirement,
  managed_evidence: EvidenceRef,
  managed_at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> BmcSecureOutcome {
  if (observed.published_user as Int) != (observed.managed_user as Int) || (derivation.account as String) != (observed.managed.account as String) {
    BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: "the derived retirement names an account the managed probe did not authenticate as" as NonEmptyStr } }
  } else if !(match observed.board {
      Absent => false
      Present { value: b } => bmc_credential_policy_key_eq(a: derivation.policy, b: BmcCredentialPolicyKey { board: b, firmware: observed.firmware })
    }) {
    BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: "the derived retirement was grounded by another board's or build's policy than the controller this reading observed" as NonEmptyStr } }
  } else {
    match observed.published_account.kind {
      PublishedAccountRetired =>
        BmcSecured {
          endpoint: observed.endpoint,
          reference: observed.managed,
          evidence: concat([managed_evidence, observed.published_account.evidence], map(derivation.surfaces, x => x.evidence)),
          latest_admitted_probe_at: observer_instant_millis(instant: managed_at),
          published_credential: observed_published_account_at_join(account: observed.published_account),
        }
      PublishedAccountDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _ } =>
        BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: "a derived retirement over an account read as disabled rather than retired" as NonEmptyStr } }
      PublishedAccountRetainedByPolicy { retention: _ } =>
        BmcSecureRefused { cause: PublishedCredentialRetirementUnestablished { detail: "a derived retirement over an account read as retained by policy" as NonEmptyStr } }
    }
  }
}

// Under a break-glass retention policy the retained account must be the goal's exact generation.
fn retention_is_goal_bound(kind: PublishedAccountKind, goal: BmcSecureGoal) -> Bool {
  match kind {
    PublishedAccountRetired => true
    PublishedAccountDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _ } => true
    PublishedAccountRetainedByPolicy { retention: r } =>
      match r {
        PublishedFactoryCredential => true
        BreakGlassAccount { secret: sec } =>
          (sec.project as String) == (goal.published_break_glass.secret.project as String)
            && sec.secret == goal.published_break_glass.secret.secret
            && sec.version == goal.published_break_glass.secret.version
      }
  }
}

fn retained_secret_or_goal(kind: PublishedAccountKind, goal: BmcSecureGoal) -> SecretRef {
  match kind {
    PublishedAccountRetired => goal.published_break_glass.secret
    PublishedAccountDisabledNotRetired { restore_path: _ } => goal.published_break_glass.secret
    PublishedAccountRetainedByPolicy { retention: r } =>
      match r {
        PublishedFactoryCredential => goal.published_break_glass.secret
        BreakGlassAccount { secret: sec } => sec
      }
  }
}

fn assess_break_glass_generation(
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  observed: BmcAccountStateObservation,
  evidence: List<EvidenceRef>,
) -> GoalAssessment<BmcSecureHeld, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateRefusal> {
  if !managed_reference_same(a: goal.published_break_glass, b: observed.break_glass) {
    GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountStateForOtherBreakGlassReference { goal: goal.published_break_glass, observed: observed.break_glass } }
  } else {
    match observed.break_glass_probe {
      ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: d } =>
        GoalIndeterminate { known_deviations: [], unknowns: FreeSemigroup { head: BreakGlassGenerationUnestablished { detail: d }, tail: [] } }
      ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: r } =>
        if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: r.observed_at, later: observed.read_floor) {
          GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountReadingPrecedesReadFloor { floor: observed.read_floor } }
        } else {
          GoalDiverged { deviations: FreeSemigroup { head: BreakGlassGenerationRejected, tail: [] } }
        }
      ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: r } =>
        if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: r.observed_at, later: observed.read_floor) {
          GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountReadingPrecedesReadFloor { floor: observed.read_floor } }
        } else {
          GoalSatisfied { evidence: BmcSecureHeld { observation: observed, evidence: concat(evidence, [r.evidence]) } }
        }
    }
  }
}

fn assess_bmc_account_state(
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  observed: BmcAccountStateObservation,
) -> GoalAssessment<BmcSecureHeld, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateRefusal> {
  if !managed_reference_same(a: goal.managed, b: observed.managed) {
    GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountStateForOtherManagedReference { goal: goal.managed, observed: observed.managed } }
  } else if !retention_is_goal_bound(kind: observed.published_account.kind, goal: goal) {
    GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountRetentionNotGoalBound { retained: retained_secret_or_goal(kind: observed.published_account.kind, goal: goal), goal: goal.published_break_glass } }
  } else {
    match conjunction_over_observation(goal: goal, observed: observed) {
      BmcSecured { endpoint: _, reference: _, evidence: e, latest_admitted_probe_at: _, published_credential: _ } =>
        assess_break_glass_generation(goal: goal, observed: observed, evidence: e)
      BmcSecureRefused { cause: c } =>
        match conjunction_cause_class(cause: c) {
          CauseRemediableByAccountAction => GoalDiverged { deviations: FreeSemigroup { head: ConjunctionFinding { cause: c }, tail: [] } }
          CauseNeedsUngroundedOperation { operation: op } => GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountDeviationNeedsUngroundedOperation { cause: c, operation: op } }
          CauseUnestablishedReading => GoalIndeterminate { known_deviations: [], unknowns: FreeSemigroup { head: ConjunctionFinding { cause: c }, tail: [] } }
          CauseReadingPrecedesFloor => GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountReadingPrecedesReadFloor { floor: observed.read_floor } }
          CauseRefusesAssessment => GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: AccountStateConjunctionRefused { cause: c } }
        }
    }
  }
}

// The observer of this effect is the supplied reading: the read itself is the realization's (dry
// below; live is bmc_secure_state_live_read_frontier), and the observer refuses a reading of another
// subject rather than assessing it.
fn observe_bmc_account_state(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  reading: BmcAccountStateObservation,
) -> ObservationAttempt<BmcAccountStateObservation, BmcSecureStateRefusal> {
  if same_intake_subject(left: subject, right: reading.subject) {
    ObservationEstablished { observed: reading }
  } else {
    ObservationRefused { cause: AccountStateForOtherSubject { expected: subject, found: reading.subject } }
  }
}

// What a divergence obliges: an account action, not yet admitted. Admission is the plan mint's.
type BmcAccountActionDue {
  deviation: BmcSecureStateFinding
}

fn decide_bmc_account_state(
  assessment: GoalAssessment<BmcSecureHeld, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateRefusal>,
) -> UpsertDecision<BmcAccountActionDue> {
  match assessment {
    GoalSatisfied { evidence: _ } => Noop
    GoalDiverged { deviations: d } => Apply { plan: BmcAccountActionDue { deviation: d.head } }
    GoalIndeterminate { known_deviations: _, unknowns: u } => Refuse { reason: bmc_secure_state_finding_label(finding: u.head) }
    GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: c } => Refuse { reason: bmc_secure_state_refusal_label(cause: c) }
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_state_refusal_label(cause: BmcSecureStateRefusal) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match cause {
    AccountStateForOtherSubject { expected: _, found: _ } => "the account-state reading belongs to another intake subject"
    AccountStateForOtherManagedReference { goal: _, observed: _ } => "the account-state reading probed another managed credential generation than the goal names"
    AccountReadingPrecedesReadFloor { floor: _ } => "an account-state reading precedes the observer instant its read began"
    AccountStateConjunctionRefused { cause: c } => bmc_secure_refusal_label(cause: c)
    AccountDeviationNeedsUngroundedOperation { cause: _, operation: op } =>
      match op {
        PublishedFactoryCredentialRestore => "the policy retains the factory credential and it is not accepted; restoring it is not an admitted operation"
      }
    AccountRetentionNotGoalBound { retained: _, goal: _ } => "the break-glass account retained by policy is not the generation the goal names"
    AccountStateForOtherBreakGlassReference { goal: _, observed: _ } => "the account-state reading probed another break-glass generation than the goal names"
  }
}

// THE EFFECT'S DOMAIN PROJECTION (gunbc.host_convergence_protocol): observe, assess, decide. Its census row
// is the arrival entry's (gunbc.host_convergence_census, arrival_converge bmc_secure), the one route
// that selects it. The protocol's apply side is an open frontier
// (host_effect_decide_apply_frontier, CONVERGENCE-ONE C8); the apply and the independent readback
// below are this domain's own, with its own sealed receipt, and do not discharge C8.
fn bmc_secure_state_projection() -> HostEffectDomainProjection<MachineIntakeSubject, BmcSecureGoal, BmcAccountStateObservation, BmcAccountStateObservation, BmcSecureHeld, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateRefusal, BmcSecureStateRefusal, BmcAccountActionDue> {
  HostEffectDomainProjection {
    observe: observe_bmc_account_state,
    assess: assess_bmc_account_state,
    decide: decide_bmc_account_state,
  }
}

type BmcSecureStateInspection
  = BmcSecureStateInspected {
      observed: BmcAccountStateObservation,
      assessment: GoalAssessment<BmcSecureHeld, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateFinding, BmcSecureStateRefusal>,
      decision: UpsertDecision<BmcAccountActionDue>,
    }
  | BmcSecureStateUnobserved { cause: BmcSecureStateRefusal }

fn inspect_bmc_secure_state(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  reading: BmcAccountStateObservation,
) -> BmcSecureStateInspection {
  let projection = bmc_secure_state_projection()
  match inspect_via_host_effect_projection(subject: subject, goal: goal, request: reading, projection: projection) {
    GoalObservationRefused { subject: _, goal: _, request: _, cause: c } => BmcSecureStateUnobserved { cause: c }
    GoalInspected { subject: _, goal: _, request: _, observed: o, assessment: a } =>
      BmcSecureStateInspected { observed: o, assessment: a, decision: projection.decide(a) }
  }
}

// ── THE SECRET ORDER, AS CARRIERS THE APPLY REQUIRES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The new credential generation is generated and STORED under the unit's SecretRef, and its EXACT
// resolved version is FETCHED, before any account write and before the managed probe. The earlier
// plan row that materialized the managed secret after BmcSecure was wrong: a rotation cannot first
// obtain its secret after it has completed. So the write's plan takes a Fetched generation, a Fetched
// generation can only be minted from a Stored one and a fetch that resolved to exactly the stored
// version, and every later consumer materializes that same generation through
// gunbc.auth.secret_ref_credential fetch_secret_ref_credential over the pinned reference the carrier
// holds. None of these carriers holds the secret bytes.

type ManagedCredentialGenerationStored sole_constructor {
  reference: ManagedCredentialReference
  stored_version: SmResolvedVersionIdentity
  stored_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

type GenerationStoreRefusal
  = GenerationStoreForAnotherSecret { expected: NonEmptyStr, stored: SmResolvedVersionIdentity }
  | GenerationStoreNotAVersionResource { supplied: String }

type GenerationStoreAdmission
  = GenerationStored { stored: ManagedCredentialGenerationStored }
  | GenerationStoreRefused { cause: GenerationStoreRefusal }

// current is the generation in force; the stored generation is the next epoch of the same account,
// role and secret, pinned to the exact version Secret Manager answered for the write (AddVersion's
// returned name), never an alias.
fn admit_stored_generation(
  current: ManagedCredentialReference,
  added: SmResolvedVersionIdentity,
  stored_at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> GenerationStoreAdmission {
  match sm_resolved_version_secret_resource(identity: added) {
    SmVersionSecretNotAVersionResource { supplied: s } => GenerationStoreRefused { cause: GenerationStoreNotAVersionResource { supplied: s } }
    SmVersionSecretProjected { secret_resource: sec } =>
      if !gcp_resource_names_this_secret(returned: sec as String, project: current.secret.project, project_number: fleet_secrets_project_number, secret: current.secret.secret) {
        GenerationStoreRefused { cause: GenerationStoreForAnotherSecret { expected: current.secret.secret, stored: added } }
      } else {
        match sm_resolved_version_id(identity: added) {
          SmVersionIdNotAVersionResource { supplied: s } => GenerationStoreRefused { cause: GenerationStoreNotAVersionResource { supplied: s } }
          SmVersionIdProjected { version: v } =>
            GenerationStored {
              stored: ManagedCredentialGenerationStored {
                reference: ManagedCredentialReference {
                  account: current.account,
                  role: current.role,
                  secret: SecretRef { project: current.secret.project, secret: current.secret.secret, version: v, hash_state: HashPending },
                  credential_epoch: current.credential_epoch + 1,
                },
                stored_version: added,
                stored_at: stored_at,
              },
            }
        }
      }
  }
}

type ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched sole_constructor {
  stored: ManagedCredentialGenerationStored
  fetched_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

type GenerationFetchRefusal
  = GenerationFetchNotReady { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | GenerationFetchResolvedAnotherVersion { stored: SmResolvedVersionIdentity, resolved: SmResolvedVersionIdentity }
  | GenerationFetchPrecedesStore { stored_at: ObserverClockInstant, fetched_at: ObserverClockInstant }

type GenerationFetchAdmission
  = GenerationFetched { fetched: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched }
  | GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchRefusal }

fn admit_fetched_generation(
  stored: ManagedCredentialGenerationStored,
  fetch: SecretCredentialFetch,
  fetched_at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> GenerationFetchAdmission {
  if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: fetched_at, later: stored.stored_at) {
    GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchPrecedesStore { stored_at: stored.stored_at, fetched_at: fetched_at } }
  } else {
    match fetch {
      SecretCredentialReady { credential: _, resolved_version: r } =>
        if (r as String) != (stored.stored_version as String) {
          GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchResolvedAnotherVersion { stored: stored.stored_version, resolved: r } }
        } else {
          GenerationFetched { fetched: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched { stored: stored, fetched_at: fetched_at } }
        }
      SecretCredentialAccessUpsertRequired { plan: _ } => GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchNotReady { detail: "secret access needs an access upsert first" as NonEmptyStr } }
      SecretCredentialWireDecodeRefused { identity_cause: _, payload_cause: _ } => GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchNotReady { detail: "secret access response did not decode" as NonEmptyStr } }
      SecretCredentialFetchRefused { reason: why } => GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchNotReady { detail: why } }
      SecretCredentialResolvedVersionMismatch { requested: _, resolved: _ } => GenerationFetchRefused { cause: GenerationFetchNotReady { detail: "secret access resolved another version than requested" as NonEmptyStr } }
    }
  }
}

// The pinned reference a later consumer passes to fetch_secret_ref_credential: the exact version, never
// the alias the generation was stored under.
fn fetched_generation_reference(fetched: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched) -> ManagedCredentialReference {
  fetched.stored.reference
}

// ── THE ACCOUNT ACTION, ADMITTED OVER A GROUNDED ROUTE ───────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Two writes, each over its own admitted route: the managed account set to the fetched managed
// generation, and the published account retired by setting it to a fetched break-glass generation the
// fleet owns (the user-2 retirement mtcollins1 executed on 2026-09-13). Each admission is COMPUTED here
// by gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_rotation_route admit_rotation_apply from the route standing, the
// controller and build being written and the operator's approval; an admission is never received.
// Every arm other than RotationApplyAdmitted refuses before any write is planned, which is what
// is that module's rotation_route_consumption_frontier consumer in code; the frontier stands until this
// planner runs on a production path (the held cut-over).

type AccountWriteTarget
  = ManagedAccountTarget
  | PublishedAccountTarget

type PlannedAccountWrite {
  target: AccountWriteTarget
  user: IpmiUserId
  route: BmcRotationRouteStanding
  request: BmcAccountWriteRequest
  decided_by: NonEmptyStr
  generation: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched
}

// THE PUBLISHED ACCOUNT'S WRITE. Separate: a distinct published account retired to the goal's break-glass
// generation by its own write. TheManagedWrite: the published login names the managed account itself
// (OpenBMC root), so the one managed write retires the published credential and a second write of the same
// account would only repeat it (DESIGN §2).
type PlannedPublishedWrite
  = PublishedWrittenSeparately { write: PlannedAccountWrite }
  | PublishedIsTheManagedWrite

// What the caller supplies for that write, in the same two shapes. Its approval is the plan's one approval.
type PublishedWriteInput
  = PublishedWriteInputs {
      route: BmcRotationRouteStanding
      generation: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched
    }
  | PublishedAccountIsTheManagedAccount

type BmcAccountActionPlan sole_constructor {
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity
  goal: BmcSecureGoal
  diverged: BmcAccountStateObservation
  due: BmcAccountActionDue
  managed_write: PlannedAccountWrite
  published_write: PlannedPublishedWrite
  channel_writes: List<PlannedChannelAccessWrite>
  planned_at: ObserverClockInstant
}
// THE FAILED-LOGIN BUDGET'S REFUSAL (the last arm) carries one entry per
// account+surface that is over budget, each with the plan's own cost, the served
// threshold, and what is already spent inside the reset window — or the reason no
// threshold could be planned against at all. See the section at the end of this
// module; the rung is
// test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_served_lockout_witness.threshold_three_refuses_three_failing_logins_and_admits_two.

type BmcAccountPlanRefusal
  = AccountPlanNotDue { decision: UpsertDecision<BmcAccountActionDue> }
  | AccountPlanUnobserved { cause: BmcSecureStateRefusal }
  | AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: AccountWriteTarget, admission: RotationApplyAdmission }
  | AccountWriteRequestForAnotherAccount { target: AccountWriteTarget, request: BmcAccountWriteRequest }
  | PublishedAccountIsNotTheManagedAccount { published_user: IpmiUserId, managed_user: IpmiUserId }
  | PublishedWriteWouldRepeatTheManagedWrite { user: IpmiUserId }
  | PublishedGoalIsNotTheManagedGoal { goal: ManagedCredentialReference, managed: ManagedCredentialReference }
  | ManagedGenerationForAnotherAccount { generation: ManagedCredentialReference, in_force: ManagedCredentialReference }
  | ManagedGenerationNotAdvanced { in_force: Int, generation: Int }
  | PublishedGenerationNotGoalBound { generation: ManagedCredentialReference, goal: ManagedCredentialReference }
  | GenerationFetchedAfterPlan { target: AccountWriteTarget, fetched_at: ObserverClockInstant, planned_at: ObserverClockInstant }
  | PlanPrecedesDivergedReading { read_floor: ObserverClockInstant, planned_at: ObserverClockInstant }
  | PlanPrecedesReading { planned_at: ObserverClockInstant }
  | ManagedUserNotTheAuthenticatedAccount { supplied: IpmiUserId, authenticated: IpmiUserId }
  | ChannelCloseRouteNotSupplied { channels: List<IpmiChannelNumber> }
  | PlanWritesAreNotTheApprovedConvergence { approved: List<BmcAccountWriteRequest>, planned: List<BmcAccountWriteRequest> }
  | ChannelWriteNotAdmitted { channel: IpmiChannelNumber, admission: RotationApplyAdmission }
  | FailedLoginBudgetExceeded { blocked: List<BmcFailedLoginBudgetBlockReading> }

type BmcAccountPlanOutcome
  = BmcAccountPlanned { plan: BmcAccountActionPlan }
  | BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: BmcAccountPlanRefusal }

// THE PASSWORD WRITE A ROUTE MAKES FOR ONE ACCOUNT. A route grounds an operation: an IPMI Set User Password
// route is written by the account's IPMI user id, a Redfish account-password route by the account's name.
// A route grounding neither password operation has no password write to offer.
fn password_write_over(route: BmcRotationRouteStanding, user: IpmiUserId, account: NonEmptyStr) -> BmcAccountWriteRequest? {
  match grounded_request(standing: route) {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: g } =>
      match g {
        IpmiSetUserPassword { user: _ } => Present { value: IpmiSetUserPassword { user: user } }
        RedfishAccountPasswordWrite { account: _, transport_operation: op, action_shape: act } =>
          Present { value: RedfishAccountPasswordWrite { account: account, transport_operation: op, action_shape: act } }
        IpmiSetUserPrivilegeLimit { access: _ } => none
      }
  }
}

// The password write a plan asks a route for: the route's own operation for this account, or, over a route
// grounding no password operation, the IPMI write its admission then refuses as another operation.
fn wanted_account_write(route: BmcRotationRouteStanding, user: IpmiUserId, account: NonEmptyStr) -> BmcAccountWriteRequest {
  match password_write_over(route: route, user: user, account: account) {
    Present { value: r } => r
    Absent => IpmiSetUserPassword { user: user }
  }
}

fn admitted_account_write(
  target: AccountWriteTarget,
  user: IpmiUserId,
  account: NonEmptyStr,
  route: BmcRotationRouteStanding,
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  approval: ScopedAuthorization<BmcAccountWriteApproval>,
  generation: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched,
  planned_at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> PlannedAccountWriteAdmission {
  let wanted = wanted_account_write(route: route, user: user, account: account)
  let admission = admit_rotation_apply(standing: route, target_endpoint: endpoint, target_firmware: firmware, request: wanted, managed_readback: none, approval: approval)
  match admission {
    RotationApplyAdmitted { standing: s, request: req, decided_by: by } =>
      if !account_write_request_eq(a: req, b: wanted) {
        PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteRequestForAnotherAccount { target: target, request: req } }
      } else if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: planned_at, later: generation.fetched_at) {
        PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: GenerationFetchedAfterPlan { target: target, fetched_at: generation.fetched_at, planned_at: planned_at } }
      } else {
        PlannedAccountWriteAdmitted {
          write: PlannedAccountWrite { target: target, user: user, route: s, request: req, decided_by: by, generation: generation },
        }
      }
    RotationApplyRouteNotGrounded { standing: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyRouteForAnotherController { route_endpoint: _, target_endpoint: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyRouteForAnotherBuild { route_firmware: _, target_firmware: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyApprovalRefused { cause: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyRouteForAnotherOperation { grounded: _, requested: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyRouteEffectUnobserved { standing: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
    RotationApplyWouldLeaveNoAdministrator { channel: _, cause: _ } => PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: AccountWriteNotAdmitted { target: target, admission: admission } }
  }
}

// ── THE CHANNEL-ACCESS WRITES (cut O1a-2) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Every census member on which the published account still holds access (its unique Get User Access
// row is not NO ACCESS) gets one privilege-limit-only Set User Access write setting it to NO
// ACCESS, over the supplied channel-access route. Each write's admission is COMPUTED by
// admit_rotation_apply: the route must be grounded with its effect observed for this controller and
// build, the approval must name this exact write, and the administrator-retention readback is
// PROJECTED here from the very observation the plan assessed -- the managed account authenticated in
// that read, and its own unique Get User Access row on the channel at ADMINISTRATOR -- never received.
type PlannedChannelAccessWrite {
  channel: IpmiChannelNumber
  route: BmcRotationRouteStanding
  request: BmcAccountWriteRequest
  decided_by: NonEmptyStr
}

type ChannelCloseInput {
  route: BmcRotationRouteStanding
}

fn census_member_channel(m: IpmiChannelCensusMember) -> IpmiChannelNumber {
  match m {
    IpmiNonLanChannelMember { channel: ch, medium: _ } => ch
    IpmiLanChannelMember { channel: ch, medium: _, ipv4: _ } => ch
  }
}

// Every census member -- LAN, addressed or not, and non-LAN such as a serial channel -- on which the
// published account's unique Get User Access row is not NO ACCESS. A missing or duplicated row is not
// listed here: the conjunction already refuses those readings before any plan. Where the published account
// IS the managed account (OpenBMC root), its access rows are the managed account's: the password write
// retires the published credential, and closing those channels would lock the managed credential out.
fn published_channels_left_open(observed: BmcAccountStateObservation) -> List<IpmiChannelNumber> {
  if observed.published_user == observed.managed_user { [] } else { published_channels_open_to(observed: observed) }
}

fn published_channels_open_to(observed: BmcAccountStateObservation) -> List<IpmiChannelNumber> {
  let index = index_published_user_access(rows: observed.channel_census.user_access)
  fold(observed.channel_census.members, init: [], f: (acc, m) =>
    match map_get(index, published_user_access_key(channel: census_member_channel(m: m), user: observed.published_user)) {
      Absent => acc
      Present { value: slot } =>
        match slot {
          SeveralUserAccess => acc
          OneUserAccess { access: row } => if row.privilege == IpmiPrivilegeNoAccess { acc } else { concat(acc, [census_member_channel(m: m)]) }
        }
    })
}

// THE PROJECTION. Present only when the observation established the managed account's authentication
// at or after its read floor and took its census at or after that floor; the access rows are the
// census's Get User Access rows for the AUTHENTICATED managed user the observation recorded, and the
// readback carries the observation's own endpoint, build and attempt -- all set by the observation's
// producer, none by a consumer. The admission then compares that attempt with the approval's, so an
// approval for another run refuses. Admitted only to admitted_channel_writes: no facade returns it.
fn project_managed_administrator_readback(observed: BmcAccountStateObservation) -> ManagedAdministratorReadback?
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "admitted_channel_writes"),
  ]
{
  match observed.managed_probe {
    ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: r } =>
      if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: r.observed_at, later: observed.read_floor) || observer_instant_precedes(earlier: observed.census_observed_at, later: observed.read_floor) {
        none
      } else {
        Present {
          value: managed_administrator_readback_projected(
            endpoint: observed.endpoint,
            firmware: observed.firmware,
            attempt: observed.attempt,
            managed_user: observed.managed_user,
            access: filter(observed.channel_census.user_access, a => (a.user as Int) == (observed.managed_user as Int)),
          ),
        }
      }
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: _ } => none
    ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: _ } => none
  }
}

fn managed_probe_instant(probe: ObservedCredentialProbe, fallback: ObserverClockInstant) -> ObserverClockInstant {
  match probe {
    ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: r } => r.observed_at
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: r } => r.observed_at
    ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: _ } => fallback
  }
}

// The supplied grant whose approved subject is this write. Its purpose and intent are read by the
// admission (read_bmc_write_approval), so a grant selected here for its subject is still refused
// there if it approves another purpose.
type ChannelWritesAdmission
  = ChannelWritesAdmitted { writes: List<PlannedChannelAccessWrite> }
  | ChannelWritesRefused { cause: BmcAccountPlanRefusal }

fn channel_close_request(observed: BmcAccountStateObservation, channel: IpmiChannelNumber) -> BmcAccountWriteRequest {
  IpmiSetUserPrivilegeLimit { access: ipmi_user_channel_access(channel: channel, user: observed.published_user, privilege: IpmiPrivilegeNoAccess) }
}

fn admitted_channel_writes(observed: BmcAccountStateObservation, input: ChannelCloseInput?, approval: ScopedAuthorization<BmcAccountWriteApproval>) -> ChannelWritesAdmission {
  let open = published_channels_left_open(observed: observed)
  if list_length(items: open) == 0 {
    ChannelWritesAdmitted { writes: [] }
  } else {
    match input {
      Absent => ChannelWritesRefused { cause: ChannelCloseRouteNotSupplied { channels: open } }
      Present { value: inp } =>
        fold(open, init: ChannelWritesAdmitted { writes: [] }, f: (acc, ch) =>
          match acc {
            ChannelWritesRefused { cause: _ } => acc
            ChannelWritesAdmitted { writes: done } => {
              let request = channel_close_request(observed: observed, channel: ch)
              let readback = project_managed_administrator_readback(observed: observed)
              let admission = admit_rotation_apply(
                standing: inp.route,
                target_endpoint: observed.endpoint,
                target_firmware: observed.firmware,
                request: request,
                managed_readback: readback,
                approval: approval,
              )
              match admission {
                RotationApplyAdmitted { standing: st, request: req, decided_by: by } =>
                  ChannelWritesAdmitted { writes: concat(done, [PlannedChannelAccessWrite { channel: ch, route: st, request: req, decided_by: by }]) }
                RotationApplyRouteNotGrounded { standing: _ } => ChannelWritesRefused { cause: ChannelWriteNotAdmitted { channel: ch, admission: admission } }
                RotationApplyRouteForAnotherController { route_endpoint: _, target_endpoint: _ } => ChannelWritesRefused { cause: ChannelWriteNotAdmitted { channel: ch, admission: admission } }
                RotationApplyRouteForAnotherBuild { route_firmware: _, target_firmware: _ } => ChannelWritesRefused { cause: ChannelWriteNotAdmitted { channel: ch, admission: admission } }
                RotationApplyRouteForAnotherOperation { grounded: _, requested: _ } => ChannelWritesRefused { cause: ChannelWriteNotAdmitted { channel: ch, admission: admission } }
                RotationApplyRouteEffectUnobserved { standing: _ } => ChannelWritesRefused { cause: ChannelWriteNotAdmitted { channel: ch, admission: admission } }
                RotationApplyApprovalRefused { cause: _ } => ChannelWritesRefused { cause: ChannelWriteNotAdmitted { channel: ch, admission: admission } }
                RotationApplyWouldLeaveNoAdministrator { channel: _, cause: _ } => ChannelWritesRefused { cause: ChannelWriteNotAdmitted { channel: ch, admission: admission } }
              }
            }
          })
    }
  }
}

type PlannedAccountWriteAdmission
  = PlannedAccountWriteAdmitted { write: PlannedAccountWrite }
  | PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: BmcAccountPlanRefusal }

// WHAT A RUN ASKS THE OPERATOR TO APPROVE: the convergence the reading entails, computed by the same
// helpers the plan admits its writes with (wanted_account_write, channel_close_request), so the request and the
// plan cannot name different writes -- and if the controller changes between the request and the plan, the
// plan's exactness check below refuses. The run files it through gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_rotation_route
// bmc_account_write_authorization_request: one request, one tap, per controller.
fn bmc_secure_convergence_approval(
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  reading: BmcAccountStateObservation,
  managed_user: IpmiUserId,
  managed_route: BmcRotationRouteStanding,
  published: PublishedWriteInput,
) -> BmcAccountWriteApproval {
  let managed = wanted_account_write(route: managed_route, user: managed_user, account: goal.managed.account)
  let published_requests: List<BmcAccountWriteRequest> = match published {
    PublishedWriteInputs { route: r, generation: _ } => [wanted_account_write(route: r, user: reading.published_user, account: goal.published_break_glass.account)]
    PublishedAccountIsTheManagedAccount => []
  }
  BmcAccountWriteApproval {
    controller: reading.endpoint,
    firmware: reading.firmware,
    writes: concat(concat([managed], published_requests), map(published_channels_left_open(observed: reading), ch => channel_close_request(observed: reading, channel: ch))),
    purpose: RotateCredential,
  }
}

// THE PLAN IS THE APPROVED CONVERGENCE, NO MORE AND NO LESS (operator ruling 2026-10-25, gunbc.design_ruling
// the_initial_convergence_is_the_only_approval). Each write was admitted against the one approval above; a
// plan that entails fewer writes than were approved is another convergence than the operator approved (the
// controller changed since the request was filed), and is refused for a fresh request rather than run in part.
fn planned_write_requests(managed: PlannedAccountWrite, published: PlannedPublishedWrite, channels: List<PlannedChannelAccessWrite>) -> List<BmcAccountWriteRequest> {
  let published_requests: List<BmcAccountWriteRequest> = match published {
    PublishedWrittenSeparately { write: w } => [w.request]
    PublishedIsTheManagedWrite => []
  }
  concat(concat([managed.request], published_requests), map(channels, c => c.request))
}

fn approved_write_requests(approval: ScopedAuthorization<BmcAccountWriteApproval>) -> List<BmcAccountWriteRequest> {
  match approval {
    AuthorizationGranted { grant: g, claim: _ } => g.subject.writes
    AuthorizationPending { request: _ } => []
    AuthorizationDenied { escalation_id: _, denied_by: _, denied_at: _, reason: _ } => []
  }
}

fn same_write_requests(a: List<BmcAccountWriteRequest>, b: List<BmcAccountWriteRequest>) -> Bool {
  length(a) == length(b)
    && all(a, x => any(b, y => account_write_request_eq(a: x, b: y)))
    && all(b, y => any(a, x => account_write_request_eq(a: x, b: y)))
}

// THE PLAN MINT RUNS THE DECISION ITSELF. A caller supplies the reading, the goal and the route
// inputs; it does not supply a decision, so an Apply cannot be planned over a Noop or a refusal.
fn plan_bmc_account_action(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  reading: BmcAccountStateObservation,
  managed_user: IpmiUserId,
  managed_route: BmcRotationRouteStanding,
  approval: ScopedAuthorization<BmcAccountWriteApproval>,
  managed_generation: ManagedCredentialGenerationFetched,
  published: PublishedWriteInput,
  channel_close: ChannelCloseInput?,
  planned_at: ObserverClockInstant,
  // WHAT THE PLAN DECLARES IT MAY DO AGAIN: each entry is a credential it may
  // present again, on one account and surface, and the budget charges every one of
  // those presentations. A plan that declares nothing is charged nothing for a
  // retry — an undeclared retry is a bug in the realization, not a licence here.
  declared_retries: List<BmcDeclaredLoginRetry>,
  // THE SEALED FORCED-CHANGE STATE of this build, if one was admitted
  // (admit_published_credential_change_forced). It is the ONLY thing that can make
  // the published credential's own authentication cost nothing, and only on the
  // Redfish surface — see bmc_plan_failing_logins.
  forced_change: PublishedCredentialChangeForced?,
) -> BmcAccountPlanOutcome {
  match inspect_bmc_secure_state(subject: subject, goal: goal, reading: reading) {
    BmcSecureStateUnobserved { cause: c } => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: AccountPlanUnobserved { cause: c } }
    BmcSecureStateInspected { observed: o, assessment: _, decision: d } =>
      match d {
        Noop => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: AccountPlanNotDue { decision: d } }
        Refuse { reason: _ } => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: AccountPlanNotDue { decision: d } }
        Apply { plan: due } =>
          if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: planned_at, later: o.read_floor) {
            BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: PlanPrecedesDivergedReading { read_floor: o.read_floor, planned_at: planned_at } }
          } else if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: planned_at, later: o.census_observed_at) || observer_instant_precedes(earlier: planned_at, later: managed_probe_instant(probe: o.managed_probe, fallback: o.read_floor)) {
            BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: PlanPrecedesReading { planned_at: planned_at } }
          } else if (managed_user as Int) != (o.managed_user as Int) {
            BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: ManagedUserNotTheAuthenticatedAccount { supplied: managed_user, authenticated: o.managed_user } }
          } else {
            let next = fetched_generation_reference(fetched: managed_generation)
            let in_force = goal.managed
            if !(next.account == in_force.account && next.role == in_force.role && (next.secret.project as String) == (in_force.secret.project as String) && next.secret.secret == in_force.secret.secret) {
              BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: ManagedGenerationForAnotherAccount { generation: next, in_force: in_force } }
            } else if next.credential_epoch <= in_force.credential_epoch {
              BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: ManagedGenerationNotAdvanced { in_force: in_force.credential_epoch, generation: next.credential_epoch } }
            } else {
              match admitted_account_write(target: ManagedAccountTarget, user: managed_user, account: in_force.account, route: managed_route, endpoint: o.endpoint, firmware: o.firmware, approval: approval, generation: managed_generation, planned_at: planned_at) {
                PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: c } => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: c }
                PlannedAccountWriteAdmitted { write: mw } =>
                  match admitted_published_write(goal: goal, observed: o, managed_user: managed_user, next: next, published: published, approval: approval, planned_at: planned_at) {
                    PublishedWriteRefused { cause: c } => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: c }
                    PublishedWriteAdmitted { write: pw, published_goal: pg } =>
                      match admitted_channel_writes(observed: o, input: channel_close, approval: approval) {
                        ChannelWritesRefused { cause: c } => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: c }
                        ChannelWritesAdmitted { writes: cw } => {
                          let planned = planned_write_requests(managed: mw, published: pw, channels: cw)
                          let approved = approved_write_requests(approval: approval)
                          if !same_write_requests(a: approved, b: planned) {
                            BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: PlanWritesAreNotTheApprovedConvergence { approved: approved, planned: planned } }
                          } else {
                            // THE FAILED-LOGIN BUDGET GATE. LAST CHECK BEFORE A PLAN IS MINTED,
                            // after the writes are admitted and after the plan is confirmed to BE
                            // the approved convergence: a plan that would spend more failed logins
                            // than this controller leaves never produces a write, never asks for an
                            // approval, and says which account on which surface is over. It sees the
                            // whole plan — managed write, published write and channel writes are all
                            // admitted by this point — because the lockout counter is spent by
                            // logins, not by writes.
                            match bmc_failed_login_budget_verdict(
                              roster: bmc_plan_failing_logins(goal: goal, observed: o, managed_write: mw, published_write: pw, forced_change: forced_change, declared_retries: declared_retries),
                              reading: o.lockout,
                              known: bmc_known_failed_logins_of(observed: o, goal: goal, managed_write: mw, published_write: pw),
                              now: observer_instant_millis(instant: planned_at),
                            ) {
                              FailedLoginBudgetRefused { blocked: blocks, spends: _, exempt: _ } => BmcAccountPlanRefused { cause: FailedLoginBudgetExceeded { blocked: blocks } }
                              FailedLoginBudgetAdmitted { spends: _, exempt: _ } =>
                                BmcAccountPlanned {
                                  plan: BmcAccountActionPlan {
                                    subject: subject,
                                    endpoint: o.endpoint,
                                    firmware: o.firmware,
                                    goal: BmcSecureGoal { managed: next, published_break_glass: pg, policy: goal.policy },
                                    diverged: o,
                                    due: due,
                                    managed_write: mw,
                                    published_write: pw,
                                    channel_writes: cw,
                                    planned_at: planned_at,
                                  },
                                }
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                  }
              }
            }
          }
      }
  }
}

type PublishedWriteAdmission
  = PublishedWriteAdmitted { write: PlannedPublishedWrite, published_goal: ManagedCredentialReference }
  | PublishedWriteRefused { cause: BmcAccountPlanRefusal }

// THE PUBLISHED ACCOUNT'S HALF OF THE PLAN, in the shape the reading allows. When the published user IS the
// managed user, only PublishedAccountIsTheManagedAccount is admitted, the goal's published generation must
// already be the managed one, and the plan's new goal carries the advanced managed generation for both
// halves -- the account has one password. When they differ, only separate inputs are admitted and the
// published write is computed as before, to the goal's predeclared break-glass generation.
fn admitted_published_write(
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  observed: BmcAccountStateObservation,
  managed_user: IpmiUserId,
  next: ManagedCredentialReference,
  published: PublishedWriteInput,
  approval: ScopedAuthorization<BmcAccountWriteApproval>,
  planned_at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> PublishedWriteAdmission {
  let same_account = (observed.published_user as Int) == (managed_user as Int)
  match published {
    PublishedAccountIsTheManagedAccount =>
      if !same_account {
        PublishedWriteRefused { cause: PublishedAccountIsNotTheManagedAccount { published_user: observed.published_user, managed_user: managed_user } }
      } else if !managed_reference_same(a: goal.published_break_glass, b: goal.managed) {
        PublishedWriteRefused { cause: PublishedGoalIsNotTheManagedGoal { goal: goal.published_break_glass, managed: goal.managed } }
      } else {
        PublishedWriteAdmitted { write: PublishedIsTheManagedWrite, published_goal: next }
      }
    PublishedWriteInputs { route: r, generation: g } =>
      if same_account {
        PublishedWriteRefused { cause: PublishedWriteWouldRepeatTheManagedWrite { user: managed_user } }
      } else if !managed_reference_same(a: fetched_generation_reference(fetched: g), b: goal.published_break_glass) {
        PublishedWriteRefused { cause: PublishedGenerationNotGoalBound { generation: fetched_generation_reference(fetched: g), goal: goal.published_break_glass } }
      } else {
        match admitted_account_write(target: PublishedAccountTarget, user: observed.published_user, account: goal.published_break_glass.account, route: r, endpoint: observed.endpoint, firmware: observed.firmware, approval: approval, generation: g, planned_at: planned_at) {
          PlannedAccountWriteRefused { cause: c } => PublishedWriteRefused { cause: c }
          PlannedAccountWriteAdmitted { write: w } => PublishedWriteAdmitted { write: PublishedWrittenSeparately { write: w }, published_goal: goal.published_break_glass }
        }
      }
  }
}

// ── THE APPLICATION RECEIPT AND THE PHASE RECEIPT ────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// What the effect did, as the realization recorded it: each write's completion, the request and
// response receipts, and the observer instant the application completed. Minted only by a realization
// of the plan in this module (the dry one below; the live one is bmc_secure_state_live_apply_frontier).
type BmcAccountApplication sole_constructor {
  plan: BmcAccountActionPlan
  managed_write_completed: Bool
  published_write_completed: Bool
  channel_writes_completed: Bool
  request_receipt: EvidenceRef
  response_receipt: EvidenceRef
  applied_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

fn apply_with_diverged_controller_clock(application: BmcAccountApplication, controller_clock: ControllerClockReading?) -> BmcAccountApplication
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "w_bmc_secure_apply_of_a_different_present_controller_clock_is_refused"),
  ]
{
  let p = application.plan
  BmcAccountApplication {
    plan: BmcAccountActionPlan {
      subject: p.subject,
      endpoint: p.endpoint,
      firmware: p.firmware,
      goal: p.goal,
      diverged: observation_with_controller_clock(base: p.diverged, controller_clock: controller_clock),
      due: p.due,
      managed_write: p.managed_write,
      published_write: p.published_write,
      channel_writes: p.channel_writes,
      planned_at: p.planned_at,
    },
    managed_write_completed: application.managed_write_completed,
    published_write_completed: application.published_write_completed,
    channel_writes_completed: application.channel_writes_completed,
    request_receipt: application.request_receipt,
    response_receipt: application.response_receipt,
    applied_at: application.applied_at,
  }
}

type BmcSecurePhaseDecision
  = BmcSecurePhaseNoop { observation: BmcAccountStateObservation }
  | BmcSecurePhaseApplied { plan: BmcAccountActionPlan, application: BmcAccountApplication, post_read: BmcAccountStateObservation }

// THE PHASE'S DOMAIN RECEIPT. gunbc.ensure says of itself that its observations and satisfaction
// Booleans are caller-supplied and that one observation can be passed twice, so the ensure shape is the
// decision only. This carrier binds subject + phase + admitted plan + application receipt +
// independent post-read + evidence, and it is sealed: its two mints below are the only constructors,
// one for a reading that already held (Noop) and one for an application followed by a readback. The
// readback is independent BY ORDERING, not by convention: its read floor must be at or after the
// application's observer instant, which is after the plan, which is after the diverged reading, so the
// pre-write reading cannot be passed as the post-read.
type BmcSecurePhaseReceipt sole_constructor {
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject
  phase: IntakePhase
  goal: BmcSecureGoal
  decision: BmcSecurePhaseDecision
  held: BmcSecureHeld
}

type BmcSecurePhaseRefusal
  = PhaseReadingUnobserved { cause: BmcSecureStateRefusal }
  | PhaseNotHeld { decision: UpsertDecision<BmcAccountActionDue> }
  | ApplicationIncomplete { managed_write_completed: Bool, published_write_completed: Bool, channel_writes_completed: Bool, response_receipt: EvidenceRef }
  | PostReadForAnotherController { expected: BmcControllerEndpoint, found: BmcControllerEndpoint }
  | PostReadPrecedesApplication { applied_at: ObserverClockInstant, read_floor: ObserverClockInstant }
  | ApplicationPrecedesPlan { planned_at: ObserverClockInstant, applied_at: ObserverClockInstant }
  | PostReadNotHeld { decision: UpsertDecision<BmcAccountActionDue> }

type BmcSecurePhaseOutcome
  = BmcSecurePhaseConverged { receipt: BmcSecurePhaseReceipt }
  | BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: BmcSecurePhaseRefusal }

fn bmc_secure_phase_noop(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  reading: BmcAccountStateObservation,
) -> BmcSecurePhaseOutcome {
  match inspect_bmc_secure_state(subject: subject, goal: goal, reading: reading) {
    BmcSecureStateUnobserved { cause: c } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PhaseReadingUnobserved { cause: c } }
    BmcSecureStateInspected { observed: o, assessment: a, decision: d } =>
      match a {
        GoalSatisfied { evidence: held } =>
          BmcSecurePhaseConverged {
            receipt: BmcSecurePhaseReceipt { subject: subject, phase: bmc_secure_phase, goal: goal, decision: BmcSecurePhaseNoop { observation: o }, held: held },
          }
        GoalDiverged { deviations: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PhaseNotHeld { decision: d } }
        GoalIndeterminate { known_deviations: _, unknowns: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PhaseNotHeld { decision: d } }
        GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PhaseNotHeld { decision: d } }
      }
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_phase_applied(
  application: BmcAccountApplication,
  post_read: BmcAccountStateObservation,
) -> BmcSecurePhaseOutcome {
  let plan = application.plan
  if !(application.managed_write_completed && application.published_write_completed && application.channel_writes_completed) {
    BmcSecurePhaseRefused {
      cause: ApplicationIncomplete {
        managed_write_completed: application.managed_write_completed,
        published_write_completed: application.published_write_completed,
        channel_writes_completed: application.channel_writes_completed,
        response_receipt: application.response_receipt,
      },
    }
  } else if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: application.applied_at, later: plan.planned_at) {
    BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: ApplicationPrecedesPlan { planned_at: plan.planned_at, applied_at: application.applied_at } }
  } else if (post_read.endpoint.host as String) != (plan.endpoint.host as String) {
    BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PostReadForAnotherController { expected: plan.endpoint, found: post_read.endpoint } }
  } else if observer_instant_precedes(earlier: post_read.read_floor, later: application.applied_at) {
    BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PostReadPrecedesApplication { applied_at: application.applied_at, read_floor: post_read.read_floor } }
  } else {
    match inspect_bmc_secure_state(subject: plan.subject, goal: plan.goal, reading: post_read) {
      BmcSecureStateUnobserved { cause: c } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PhaseReadingUnobserved { cause: c } }
      BmcSecureStateInspected { observed: o, assessment: a, decision: d } =>
        match a {
          GoalSatisfied { evidence: held } =>
            BmcSecurePhaseConverged {
              receipt: BmcSecurePhaseReceipt {
                subject: plan.subject,
                phase: bmc_secure_phase,
                goal: plan.goal,
                decision: BmcSecurePhaseApplied { plan: plan, application: application, post_read: o },
                held: held,
              },
            }
          GoalDiverged { deviations: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PostReadNotHeld { decision: d } }
          GoalIndeterminate { known_deviations: _, unknowns: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PostReadNotHeld { decision: d } }
          GoalAssessmentRefused { cause: _ } => BmcSecurePhaseRefused { cause: PostReadNotHeld { decision: d } }
        }
    }
  }
}

fn bmc_secure_phase_receipt_evidence(receipt: BmcSecurePhaseReceipt) -> List<EvidenceRef> {
  match receipt.decision {
    BmcSecurePhaseNoop { observation: _ } => receipt.held.evidence
    BmcSecurePhaseApplied { plan: _, application: a, post_read: _ } =>
      concat([a.request_receipt, a.response_receipt], receipt.held.evidence)
  }
}

// THE ONE PROJECTION FROM THIS FOLD TO THE STANDING EVERY CONSUMER READS.
//
// WHY IT EXISTS. BmcSecureStanding is what gunbc.host.managed_host, gunbc.host.bmc_control_binding,
// gunbc.host.managed_host_boot_federation, gunbc.fleet.mtcollins_firmware_converge and
// gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_bmc_secure_observation all read; before this fn its only mint took the
// EVENT-shaped BmcCredentialRotationObservation, so a controller this fold converged could not be handed
// to any of them. That is what made mtcollins1's cutover a rewrite of every consumer instead of a change
// of mint (operator ruling gunbc.design_ruling bmc_secure_goes_live_per_controller_family); with this
// projection the cutover moves the call site beside the standing, which is the flag switch
// bmc_secure_state_cutover_frontier names. It is a MINT, not a codec: a caller can hand it a receipt
// belonging to another unit and get a refused standing, and it can hand it nothing else.
//
// THE RUNG (§4b), and what the projection does NOT trust. The standing's credential verdict is RE-DERIVED
// here by conjunction_over_observation over the readback the receipt itself carries -- the observation the
// fold inspected and then had to satisfy -- so the projection cannot be talked into a BmcSecured standing
// by an argument it is handed; a reading that does not conjoin yields BmcSecureRefused with the cause the
// conjunction named, never a standing with a satisfied result. The one fact taken from the receipt rather
// than re-derived is its EVIDENCE, on the conjunction's own authority: the conjunction's list is a prefix
// of BmcSecureHeld.evidence, which bmc_secure_phase_receipt_evidence extends with the write receipts the
// Applied arm rests on -- the event path's standing carries the same two kinds, its bootstrap probe being
// the entry this fold has no route to (see the asymmetry note on the standing above). It is one authority,
// not two: the receipt mints held and the observation together, and the standing reports exactly what
// that readback established.
//
// SUBJECT, AND WHY IT IS THE ONLY CHECK. `subject` is the caller's claim and is compared against the
// subject the fold minted the receipt for -- two values minted independently, so a real check that can
// fail (the discriminating RED is the state witness's a_receipt_for_another_subject_never_projects). The
// readback's OWN subject is not compared: observe_bmc_account_state already refuses a reading of another
// unit and bmc_secure_phase_applied already refuses a post-read of another plan, so a second comparison
// there is a structural invariant dressed as a check (DESIGN §3c). The POLICY is not a formal either: the
// standing reports the policy the readback was adjudicated under, receipt.goal.policy, because a caller-
// supplied policy would be a second minted authority over the same fact and the ProdRisk arm of the
// conjunction is decided by it -- a standing claiming a policy the readback never established is the
// content-hash lie the standing's doc comment above exists to forbid. The check that would have been
// needed with such a formal is therefore not available by construction, which is the stronger answer.
//
// THE WITNESSES, AND THE FRONTIER. Positive control and the two REDs are
// test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_state_witness on the dry world, and the seal that
// keeps this the only route from a receipt to a standing is
// test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_standing_forged_probe_witness. It has no production
// caller: bmc_secure_standing_consumer_frontier below names the first.
fn bmc_secure_standing_of_phase_receipt(
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  receipt: BmcSecurePhaseReceipt,
) -> BmcSecureStanding
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_state_witness", decl_name: "the_secured_noop_projects_to_a_secured_standing"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_state_witness", decl_name: "the_secured_apply_projects_to_a_secured_standing_carrying_the_writes"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_state_witness", decl_name: "an_unestablished_reading_yields_no_receipt_to_project"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_state_witness", decl_name: "a_receipt_for_another_subject_never_projects"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_state_witness", decl_name: "the_standing_reports_the_policy_the_readback_was_adjudicated_under")
  ]
{
  let outcome =
    if !same_intake_subject(left: subject, right: receipt.subject) {
      BmcSecureRefused {
        cause: PhaseReceiptForAnotherSubject { expected: subject, found: receipt.subject },
      }
    } else {
      let readback = match receipt.decision {
        BmcSecurePhaseNoop { observation: o } => o
        BmcSecurePhaseApplied { plan: _, application: _, post_read: o } => o
      }
      match conjunction_over_observation(goal: receipt.goal, observed: readback) {
        BmcSecured {
          endpoint: endpoint,
          reference: reference,
          evidence: _,
          latest_admitted_probe_at: latest_admitted_probe_at,
          published_credential: published_credential,
        } =>
          BmcSecured {
            endpoint: endpoint,
            reference: reference,
            evidence: bmc_secure_phase_receipt_evidence(receipt: receipt),
            latest_admitted_probe_at: latest_admitted_probe_at,
            published_credential: published_credential,
          }
        BmcSecureRefused { cause: cause } => BmcSecureRefused { cause: cause }
      }
    }
  BmcSecureStanding { subject: subject, policy: receipt.goal.policy, outcome: outcome }
}

// ── THE DRY REALIZATION OVER gunbc.bmc_model BmcWorld ────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The executing consumer of this section while it is in shadow. The world's IPMI user table is the
// controller; the realization writes it through bmc_ipmi_set_user_password and reads it through
// bmc_ipmi_user_accepts, so the readback is a property of the world after the write and never the
// write's own completion. The channel census and the published user's channel access are inputs of
// the read (BmcWorld does not model channels); the probes against every addressable LAN member are
// derived from the world. The secret bytes each write uses are materialized through a
// SecretCredentialFetch that must resolve to exactly the generation the plan carries.

data bmc_secure_dry_realization_name: NonEmptyStr = "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure dry realization over gunbc.bmc_model BmcWorld" as NonEmptyStr

// THE DRY REALIZATION'S OBSERVER SCHEDULE, SEALED. An EpochMs is turned into a sealed observer instant
// only on behalf of the dry read and the dry apply, which are themselves admitted only to the named
// witness callers: the seed does not refuse a record at an EpochMs formal (gunbc#13385), so these admit
// lists are the only wall between a supplied number and a sealed instant.
fn dry_bmc_account_instant(millis: EpochMs) -> ObserverClockInstant
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "dry_read_bmc_account_state"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "dry_apply_bmc_account_plan"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "mtjade1_fetched_generation"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "mtjade1_dry_applied_bmc"),
  ]
{
  observer_clock_modeled(millis: millis, realization: bmc_secure_dry_realization_name)
}

fn dry_evidence(text: String) -> EvidenceRef {
  EvidenceRef { label: text as NonEmptyStr, digest: content_hash_of_value(value: text) }
}

fn dry_probe(world: BmcWorld, user: IpmiUserId, password: String, what: String, at: ObserverClockInstant) -> ObservedCredentialProbe
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "dry_published_lan_probes"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "dry_read_bmc_account_state"),
  ]
{
  let text = join(["dry ipmi probe ", what, " user ", to_string(user as Int), " at ", to_string(observer_instant_millis(instant: at) as Int)], "")
  if bmc_ipmi_user_accepts(world: world, user: user, password: password) {
    ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: observed_reading(evidence: dry_evidence(text: concat(text, " -> accepted")), observed_at: at) }
  } else {
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: observed_reading(evidence: dry_evidence(text: concat(text, " -> rejected")), observed_at: at) }
  }
}

fn dry_published_lan_probes(
  world: BmcWorld,
  census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_password: String,
  at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> List<ObservedPublishedLanProbe>
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "dry_published_credential"),
  ]
{
  fold(census.members, init: [], f: (acc, m) =>
    match m {
      IpmiNonLanChannelMember { channel: _, medium: _ } => acc
      IpmiLanChannelMember { channel: ch, medium: _, ipv4: cfg } =>
        match cfg {
          IpmiLanIpv4Unassigned => acc
          IpmiLanIpv4Assigned { address: a } =>
            concat(acc, [ObservedPublishedLanProbe { channel: ch, address: a, probe: dry_probe(world: world, user: published_user, password: published_password, what: "published", at: at) }])
        }
    })
}

// HOW THE DRY READ ESTABLISHES THE PUBLISHED CREDENTIAL: by probing it on every addressed LAN member, or
// by deriving its retirement on the managed account under a credential-policy row, for the surfaces the
// modeled controller serves. The dry world keeps one password per IPMI user, so a derivation over it is
// exactly as sound as the row it cites -- which is why the row, not the world, is what it names.
type DryPublishedReading
  = DryProbePublished
  | DryDerivePublishedRetirement { published_account: NonEmptyStr, served: List<CredentialSurface> }

// A derivation the policy refuses is read as an unestablished published state on the one LAN member the
// probes would have covered first, never as a retirement. The policy key is the read's own board and build.
fn dry_published_credential(
  world: BmcWorld,
  board: BoardAuthorityRef?,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  managed: ManagedCredentialReference,
  managed_password: String,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_password: String,
  reading: DryPublishedReading,
  at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> PublishedCredentialEvidence
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure", decl_name: "dry_read_bmc_account_state"),
  ]
{
  match reading {
    DryProbePublished =>
      PublishedCredentialProbed { probes: dry_published_lan_probes(world: world, census: census, published_user: published_user, published_password: published_password, at: at) }
    DryDerivePublishedRetirement { published_account: acct, served: sv } => {
      let unestablished = PublishedCredentialProbed {
        probes: map(dry_published_lan_probes(world: world, census: census, published_user: published_user, published_password: published_password, at: at), x =>
          ObservedPublishedLanProbe { channel: x.channel, address: x.address, probe: ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: "the published retirement could not be derived under the controller's credential policy" as NonEmptyStr } }),
      }
      match board {
        Absent => unestablished
        Present { value: b } =>
          match derive_shared_store_retirement(policy: BmcCredentialPolicyKey { board: b, firmware: firmware }, published_account: acct, managed_account: managed.account, served: sv, generation_is_published_password: managed_password == published_password) {
            SharedStoreRetirementDerived { derivation: d } => PublishedCredentialRetiredOnTheManagedAccount { derivation: d }
            SharedStoreRetirementRefused { cause: _ } => unestablished
          }
      }
    }
  }
}

// ONE READ OF THE WORLD'S ACCOUNT STATE. read_at_millis is the realization's observer schedule; every
// reading in the observation is taken at it. The census MEMBERS (which channels exist, their media and
// LAN addresses) are the supplied channel layout; every Get User Access row is read from the world, so a
// readback after a channel-access write reports what the write did. managed_user is the IPMI user the
// managed probe authenticated as, and attempt is the run this read belongs to: both are recorded here,
// by the producer, and never assigned later by a consumer.
fn dry_read_bmc_account_state(
  world: BmcWorld,
  subject: MachineIntakeSubject,
  endpoint: BmcControllerEndpoint,
  board: BoardAuthorityRef?,
  firmware: BmcFirmwareReleaseIdentity,
  managed: ManagedCredentialReference,
  managed_user: IpmiUserId,
  managed_password: String,
  census: IpmiControllerChannelCensus,
  published_user: IpmiUserId,
  published_password: String,
  published_account: PublishedAccountKind,
  break_glass: ManagedCredentialReference,
  break_glass_password: String,
  // THE LOCKOUT READ OF THIS PASS, taken beside the probes below. A live reader
  // fills it from a Redfish GET of AccountService and a Get LAN Configuration
  // Parameters of the addressed channel, through bmc_lockout_surface_from_redfish
  // and bmc_lockout_surface_from_ipmi_lan; until that read is wired
  // (bmc_served_lockout_live_read_frontier) every caller says so in the reading it
  // passes — test.fixture.machine_intake.bmc_lockout is how a witness does it — and
  // the budget gate then refuses any plan carrying a potentially-failing login on
  // the unread surface. It is an argument and not a default precisely because a
  // caller must decide which of those two it is.
  lockout: BmcControllerLockoutReading,
  published_reading: DryPublishedReading,
  attempt: AttemptIdentity,
  read_at_millis: EpochMs,
) -> BmcAccountStateObservation
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_state_witness", decl_name: "read_in"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_shared_store_witness", decl_name: "read_root"),
    // The served-lockout witness reads a root state so its budget gate has a real
    // observation to refuse or admit; its pass is dry and it names itself in every
    // instant it mints.
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_served_lockout_witness", decl_name: "read_lock"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_shared_store_witness", decl_name: "read_root_on"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "w_mtjade1_converges_through_bmc_secure_noop_on_the_real_prefix"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "w_mtjade1_bmc_secure_apply_inputs_missing_refuses_on_the_real_path"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "mtjade1_dry_applied_bmc"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "w_bmc_secure_apply_for_a_later_break_glass_generation_is_refused"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "w_bmc_secure_apply_of_another_channel_state_is_refused"),
  ]
{
  let at = dry_bmc_account_instant(millis: read_at_millis)
  observed_bmc_account_state(
    subject: subject,
    endpoint: endpoint,
    board: board,
    firmware: firmware,
    managed: managed,
    managed_user: managed_user,
    attempt: attempt,
    read_floor: at,
    managed_probe: dry_probe(world: world, user: managed_user, password: managed_password, what: "managed", at: at),
    channel_census: ipmi_controller_channel_census(members: census.members, user_access: world.ipmi_user_access),
    census_evidence: dry_evidence(text: join(["dry channel census of ", endpoint.host as String, " at ", to_string(read_at_millis as Int)], "")),
    census_observed_at: at,
    published_credential: dry_published_credential(world: world, board: board, firmware: firmware, census: census, managed: managed, managed_password: managed_password, published_user: published_user, published_password: published_password, reading: published_reading, at: at),
    published_user: published_user,
    published_account: observed_published_account(
      kind: published_account,
      evidence: dry_evidence(text: join(["dry user list of ", endpoint.host as String, " at ", to_string(read_at_millis as Int)], "")),
      observed_at: at,
    ),
    break_glass: break_glass,
    break_glass_probe: dry_probe(world: world, user: published_user, password: break_glass_password, what: "break-glass", at: at),
    controller_clock: none,
    lockout: lockout,
  )
}

type BmcChannelWritesDryStep {
  world: BmcWorld
  completed: Bool
}

type BmcAccountDryStep {
  world: BmcWorld
  application: BmcAccountApplication
}

fn published_write_text(write: PlannedPublishedWrite) -> String {
  match write {
    PublishedIsTheManagedWrite => "the published account, which is the managed account (no second write)"
    PublishedWrittenSeparately { write: w } => account_write_request_text(request: w.request) as String
  }
}

fn dry_fetch_resolves(fetch: SecretCredentialFetch, write: PlannedAccountWrite) -> String? {
  match fetch {
    SecretCredentialReady { credential: c, resolved_version: r } =>
      if (r as String) == (write.generation.stored.stored_version as String) { Present { value: c as String } } else { none }
    SecretCredentialAccessUpsertRequired { plan: _ } => none
    SecretCredentialWireDecodeRefused { identity_cause: _, payload_cause: _ } => none
    SecretCredentialFetchRefused { reason: _ } => none
    SecretCredentialResolvedVersionMismatch { requested: _, resolved: _ } => none
  }
}

// THE WRITES, IN THE SECRET ORDER. Each write's bytes come from a fetch that resolved to exactly that
// write's generation; a fetch of any other version writes nothing, and the application records the
// write as not completed rather than writing a different credential.
fn dry_apply_bmc_account_plan(
  world: BmcWorld,
  plan: BmcAccountActionPlan,
  managed_fetch: SecretCredentialFetch,
  published_fetch: SecretCredentialFetch,
  applied_at_millis: EpochMs,
) -> BmcAccountDryStep
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_state_witness", decl_name: "applied_outcome_of_plan"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_shared_store_witness", decl_name: "the_root_rotation_applies_reads_back_and_converges"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_state_witness", decl_name: "the_post_read_is_independent_of_the_reading_that_diverged"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_secure_state_witness", decl_name: "a_planned_channel_close_is_applied_read_back_and_converges"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_arrival_converge_witness", decl_name: "mtjade1_dry_applied_bmc"),
  ]
{
  // A Redfish account-password write and an IPMI Set User Password land in the dry world the same way: the
  // world keeps one password per user, which is the shared-store premise a derived retirement cites.
  let managed_step = match dry_fetch_resolves(fetch: managed_fetch, write: plan.managed_write) {
    Absent => BmcIpmiSetUserPasswordStep { world: world, completed: false }
    Present { value: pw } => bmc_ipmi_set_user_password(world: world, user: plan.managed_write.user, password: pw)
  }
  let published_step = match plan.published_write {
    PublishedIsTheManagedWrite => BmcIpmiSetUserPasswordStep { world: managed_step.world, completed: managed_step.completed }
    PublishedWrittenSeparately { write: w } =>
      match dry_fetch_resolves(fetch: published_fetch, write: w) {
        Absent => BmcIpmiSetUserPasswordStep { world: managed_step.world, completed: false }
        Present { value: pw } => bmc_ipmi_set_user_password(world: managed_step.world, user: w.user, password: pw)
      }
  }
  let channel_steps = fold(plan.channel_writes, init: BmcChannelWritesDryStep { world: published_step.world, completed: true }, f: (acc, w) =>
    match w.request {
      IpmiSetUserPrivilegeLimit { access: x } => {
        let step = bmc_ipmi_set_user_access(world: acc.world, access: x)
        BmcChannelWritesDryStep { world: step.world, completed: acc.completed && step.completed }
      }
      IpmiSetUserPassword { user: _ } => BmcChannelWritesDryStep { world: acc.world, completed: false }
      RedfishAccountPasswordWrite { account: _, transport_operation: _, action_shape: _ } => BmcChannelWritesDryStep { world: acc.world, completed: false }
    })
  let request_text = join(
    concat(
      ["dry ", account_write_request_text(request: plan.managed_write.request) as String, " then ", published_write_text(write: plan.published_write)],
      concat(map(plan.channel_writes, w => concat(" then ", account_write_request_text(request: w.request) as String)), [" on ", plan.endpoint.host as String]),
    ),
    "",
  )
  let response_text = join(
    [request_text, " -> managed completed=", if managed_step.completed { "true" } else { "false" }, " published completed=", if published_step.completed { "true" } else { "false" }, " channel writes completed=", if channel_steps.completed { "true" } else { "false" }],
    "",
  )
  BmcAccountDryStep {
    world: channel_steps.world,
    application: BmcAccountApplication {
      plan: plan,
      managed_write_completed: managed_step.completed,
      published_write_completed: published_step.completed,
      channel_writes_completed: channel_steps.completed,
      request_receipt: dry_evidence(text: request_text),
      response_receipt: dry_evidence(text: response_text),
      applied_at: dry_bmc_account_instant(millis: applied_at_millis),
    },
  }
}

// ── DECLARED FRONTIERS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

data bmc_secure_state_live_read_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "dissolves when a live read of a controller's account state mints BmcAccountStateObservation beside dry_read_bmc_account_state from IPMI user-test and channel-census transport calls, including the user test of the published account with the goal's exact break-glass generation (break_glass_probe) materialized through fetch_secret_ref_credential, timed by gunbc.clock_read observer_clock_read, with every probe and census response committed as content-addressed evidence; NOT satisfied by the dry realization, by a transcription of an older readback, or by a read whose instants come from the controller's clock" as NonEmptyStr,
)

data bmc_secure_state_live_apply_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "dissolves when a live realization of BmcAccountActionPlan mints BmcAccountApplication beside dry_apply_bmc_account_plan, materializing each write's bytes through gunbc.auth.secret_ref_credential fetch_secret_ref_credential over that write's pinned generation reference, under the controller's own operator go-ahead admitted through gunbc.auth.approval_gate (gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_rotation_route read_bmc_write_approval); NOT satisfied by the dry realization, by a workflow entry that has not executed, or by a write whose bytes were supplied out of band" as NonEmptyStr,
)

// THE HELD TRANSITION (operator ruling C, 2026-10-04). Its rung drop is
// gunbc.rung_drop.mtcollins1_bmc_secure_standing_predates_reflash, retired by the same trigger.
data bmc_secure_state_cutover_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "dissolves when mtcollins1's BmcSecure standing is derived by the state-shaped fold (bmc_secure_phase_noop or bmc_secure_phase_applied) from a committed post-reflash readback of the current subject, and the rotation-event path (derive_bmc_secure, BmcCredentialRotationObservation, CredentialRotationApplication, CredentialProbeOutcome and every consumer that reads them, including gunbc.host.managed_host managed_hosts and gunbc.fleet.mtcollins_firmware_converge BmcCredentialReestablishment) is deleted in the same change; NOT satisfied by this section typechecking, by its dry realization, by re-expressing the 2026-09-13 readback on BMC 0.32, or by a readback whose subject is not the unit's current firmware" as NonEmptyStr,
)

// THE CONSUMER FRONTIER OF THE PROJECTION (DESIGN §3c). bmc_secure_standing_of_phase_receipt exists today
// with NO production caller: the event path is FROZEN, so no consumer swapped when this projection landed
// and the fold stays in shadow behind its dry realization. This row is what keeps a mint with no consumer
// from being dead code, and it names the order the consumers arrive in, so a swap can be checked against
// a promise made before it.
//
// TRIGGER, in this order, each part required:
//   1. the srv1-4 / srv14 ALTRAD8UD rows -- gunbc.host.managed_host managed_hosts rows for the units on
//      board gunbc.boards.altrad8ud (OpenBMC 03.22.00) -- are admitted with their secure standing produced
//      by bmc_secure_standing_of_phase_receipt over THAT unit's own converged phase receipt: today the
//      dry-realized fold (dry_read_bmc_account_state, dry_apply_bmc_account_plan), and the wet fold only
//      once bmc_secure_state_live_read_frontier and bmc_secure_state_live_apply_frontier have dissolved.
//      The author of that admission is added to the projection's admit_callers, which is what makes the
//      swap visible at the seal rather than in a comment.
//   2. mtcollins1's held transition follows on the SAME projection:
//      gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_bmc_secure_observation mtcollins1_bmc_secure_standing stops calling
//      derive_bmc_secure and calls this fn over the post-reflash fold's receipt, in the change that drops
//      gunbc.rung_drop.mtcollins1_bmc_secure_standing_predates_reflash.
//
// NOT satisfied by: a witness calling the projection (the witnesses are the shadow and are admitted from
// the first commit), by a consumer that re-mints the standing from an event-shaped observation, or by
// pointing a consumer at a receipt belonging to another unit or an older firmware than the standing
// claims -- the projection refuses the first and the rung drop names the second. SUFFICIENT FOR: deleting
// this row. NOT sufficient for deleting the event-path fold, which dissolves only with
// bmc_secure_state_cutover_frontier beside it, in the change that deletes that fold and its consumers.
data bmc_secure_standing_consumer_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "dissolves when the srv1-4 / srv14 ALTRAD8UD gunbc.host.managed_host rows take their BmcSecureStanding from bmc_secure_standing_of_phase_receipt over each unit's own converged BmcSecurePhaseReceipt, that admission being named in the projection's admit_callers, and mtcollins1's held transition follows on the same projection in the change that drops gunbc.rung_drop.mtcollins1_bmc_secure_standing_predates_reflash; NOT satisfied by a witness calling the projection, by a standing re-minted from an event-shaped observation, or by a consumer pointed at a receipt for another subject" as NonEmptyStr,
)

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SERVED LOCKOUT POLICY AND THE FAILED-LOGIN BUDGET (BMC 1b).
//
// WHAT THIS SECTION IS FOR. A rotation plan logs in, and a wrong password is a
// FAILED login. The controller counts failed logins per account and locks the
// account when the count reaches the threshold it SERVES — it is the controller
// that decides, not a row we keep: Redfish serves
// AccountService.AccountLockoutThreshold / AccountLockoutDuration /
// AccountLockoutCounterResetAfter / AccountLockoutCounterResetEnabled
// (extdeps.bmc.redfish, RedfishAccountServiceLockoutServed, whose module
// comment quotes each property verbatim from
// redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/AccountService.v1_19_0.json, fetched 2026-10-29),
// and an IPMI controller serves the per-channel Bad Password Threshold block of
// its LAN configuration parameters (extdeps.bmc.ipmi_channel,
// IpmiLanBadPasswordThreshold: Get LAN Configuration Parameters, NetFn 0x0C,
// parameter selector IPMI_LANP_BAD_PASS_THRESH, a 6-byte block in units of ten
// seconds — cited there from ipmitool's lib/ipmi_lanp.c at commit
// be11d948f89b10be094e28d8a0a5e8fb532c7b60, the transport this fold drives). So
// this section holds NO threshold of its own: it holds the READING of those
// served properties and the arithmetic that reading licenses. On OpenBMC the
// published account IS the managed account (root), so one careless probe locks
// the account the whole plan exists to keep; on the H11SSL units an IPMI LAN
// lockout after 3 bad passwords is what the operator reports, and that number
// is in this repository's capture
// (artifacts/bmc/h11ssl-unit1-ipmitool-2026-10-27/lan-print-1.txt:
// "Bad Password Threshold : 3") as a REPORTED read, not as a row.
//
// THE BUDGET. Every login a plan MAY make that can be answered with a rejected
// password is counted, per account AND per surface, against the headroom the
// served threshold leaves:
//
//     may_fail = threshold - 1 - (known failed attempts still inside the reset
//                window), floored at zero
//
// The -1 is because a login is refused when the count REACHES the threshold:
// with threshold 3, two failures leave the account usable and the third locks
// it. The witness test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_served_lockout_witness.threshold_three_refuses_three_failing_logins_and_admits_two is
// the rung — threshold N with a plan of N potentially-failing logins on that
// account+surface refuses, and N-1 admits — which is the same N-1 rule the
// 03.22.00 probe budget already states (bmc_probe_budget_is_sound cites the
// sealed 1 <= probes <= threshold - 1 from
// artifacts/bmc/srv15-lab-2026-10-27/openbmc-3.22.00-ipmi-probe-policy.json).
// A plan whose count exceeds the headroom is REFUSED AT PLAN TIME, inside
// plan_bmc_account_action: no write is asked for, no approval is spent, and the
// refusal is a typed BmcAccountPlanRefusal the operator reads.
//
// UNKNOWN THRESHOLD REFUSES. When a surface's threshold is not readable, no
// headroom can be computed, so ANY plan containing a potentially-failing login
// on that account+surface is refused (BmcFailedLoginThresholdUnknown) — §5,
// "what is not read is said": the safe default is the refusal, never a number.
// The ONE exception is the forced-change path, which is NOT a failed login: on
// OpenBMC 03.22.00 a login with any password is answered
// 403 Base.1.16.0.PasswordChangeRequired — an AUTHENTICATED response that
// rejects the OPERATION, not a 401 that rejects the CREDENTIAL. Only a rejected
// credential moves the controller's failed-login counter, so that path costs
// zero. That reading is not ours to assert: it is the sealed
// PublishedCredentialChangeForced of gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_credential_policy
// (minted only by admit_published_credential_change_forced, over a captured
// Redfish error body verified against the build's row), and it is grounded for
// the REDFISH surface only — the IPMI lanplus row of that same build is
// explicitly not grounded there. So the exemption is granted on the Redfish
// surface and nowhere else; the witness
// test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_served_lockout_witness.the_forced_change_path_costs_no_failed_login_on_the_surface_it_is_grounded_for is the rung
// that holds it to that scope: the same published-credential login under the
// same sealed state admits over Redfish and refuses over IPMI lanplus.
//
// WHAT COSTS WHAT.
//   - Derived retirement (PublishedCredentialRetiredOnTheManagedAccount) costs
//     ZERO failed logins: nothing is probed to prove the published password
//     fails, because the build grounds one password per account and the
//     derivation (SharedStoreRetirement) is itself the proof. Rung:
//     test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_served_lockout_witness.derived_retirement_costs_nothing_and_the_probed_path_one_per_member.
//   - The PROBED path costs ONE login per LAN member the published user may
//     reach: the plan must try the published password on each addressed LAN
//     channel (admitted_channel_writes refuses a member the plan does not
//     cover), and each attempt can be rejected. Rung:
//     test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_served_lockout_witness.derived_retirement_costs_nothing_and_the_probed_path_one_per_member.
//   - A probe is charged to the account it AUTHENTICATES AS. Probing the
//     published/ADMIN account does not spend root's budget; it spends the ADMIN
//     account's own. Rung:
//     test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_served_lockout_witness.a_retry_on_another_account_spends_that_account_and_not_root.
//   - Declared retries (BmcDeclaredLoginRetry) count: the plan says how many
//     further times it may present a credential, and each further presentation
//     is another login the controller may count. A plan that declares no retry
//     spends nothing for one — an undeclared retry is a bug in the realization,
//     not a licence handed out here. Rung:
//     test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_served_lockout_witness.declared_retries_are_charged_as_logins.
//   - A WRITE authentication is NOT counted, and that exclusion is named:
//     bmc_write_authentication_failed_login_frontier at the end of this section
//     states what would make it wrong. The password write's authorization was
//     checked before the request was built, and by the time it runs the same
//     credential has just been accepted by the probe beside it.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ── SURFACE AND KEY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The controller counts failed logins per ACCOUNT, and each surface reaches an
// account through its own code path with its own SERVED policy (the Redfish
// AccountService properties vs the per-channel IPMI LAN parameters), so the
// budget key is the PAIR: a plan may have headroom on Redfish and none on
// channel 1, and both have to be satisfied.
//
// WHY A CHANNEL AND ALSO AN UNDETERMINED ARM. The IPMI Bad Password Threshold is
// served PER CHANNEL, so a probe recorded against a channel is charged to that
// channel's counter. A plan-side IPMI login is different: the Set User Password
// request (BmcAccountWriteRequest.IpmiSetUserPassword) names a user id and no
// channel, because the lanplus transport picks the addressed channel, not the
// plan. Such a login is therefore charged to IpmiLanPlusLoginChannelUndetermined,
// whose threshold is the TIGHTEST served one across the controller's addressed
// LAN channels — the plan has to fit whichever channel it ends up crossing, and
// we do not get to choose after the fact. SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined is
// the fail-closed arm for a write whose route carries no request at all; it is
// never readable, so a login charged there is refused.

type BmcFailedLoginSurface =
    RedfishAccountServiceLogin
  | IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | IpmiLanPlusLoginChannelUndetermined
  | SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined

fn bmc_failed_login_surface_same(a: BmcFailedLoginSurface, b: BmcFailedLoginSurface) -> Bool {
  match a {
    RedfishAccountServiceLogin => match b { RedfishAccountServiceLogin => true, IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: _ } => false, IpmiLanPlusLoginChannelUndetermined => false, SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined => false }
    IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: ca } => match b {
      RedfishAccountServiceLogin => false
      IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: cb } => (ca as Int) == (cb as Int)
      IpmiLanPlusLoginChannelUndetermined => false
      SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined => false
    }
    IpmiLanPlusLoginChannelUndetermined => match b { RedfishAccountServiceLogin => false, IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: _ } => false, IpmiLanPlusLoginChannelUndetermined => true, SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined => false }
    SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined => match b { RedfishAccountServiceLogin => false, IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: _ } => false, IpmiLanPlusLoginChannelUndetermined => false, SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined => true }
  }
}

type BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey {
  account: NonEmptyStr
  surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface
}

fn bmc_failed_login_budget_key_same(a: BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey, b: BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey) -> Bool {
  (a.account as String) == (b.account as String) && bmc_failed_login_surface_same(a: a.surface, b: b.surface)
}

// ── WHAT ONE PLAN MAY LOG IN WITH ────────────────────────────────────────────
// One potentially-failing login the plan may make. Each variant names the
// account it AUTHENTICATES AS and the surface it crosses: the account is whose
// counter the controller moves, so a probe of the published ADMIN account moves
// the ADMIN's counter and not root's, whatever motivated it.

type BmcCountedFailedLogin =
    ManagedProbeLogin { account: NonEmptyStr, surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface }
  | BreakGlassProbeLogin { account: NonEmptyStr, surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface }
  | PublishedProbeLogin { account: NonEmptyStr, surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface, channel: IpmiChannelNumber }
  | PublishedCredentialAuthenticationLogin { account: NonEmptyStr, surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface }
  | DeclaredRetryLogin { account: NonEmptyStr, surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface, of: NonEmptyStr }

fn bmc_counted_login_surface(login: BmcCountedFailedLogin) -> BmcFailedLoginSurface {
  match login {
    ManagedProbeLogin { account: _, surface: s } => s
    BreakGlassProbeLogin { account: _, surface: s } => s
    PublishedProbeLogin { account: _, surface: s, channel: _ } => s
    PublishedCredentialAuthenticationLogin { account: _, surface: s } => s
    DeclaredRetryLogin { account: _, surface: s, of: _ } => s
  }
}

fn bmc_counted_login_account(login: BmcCountedFailedLogin) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match login {
    ManagedProbeLogin { account: a, surface: _ } => a
    BreakGlassProbeLogin { account: a, surface: _ } => a
    PublishedProbeLogin { account: a, surface: _, channel: _ } => a
    PublishedCredentialAuthenticationLogin { account: a, surface: _ } => a
    DeclaredRetryLogin { account: a, surface: _, of: _ } => a
  }
}

fn bmc_counted_login_key(login: BmcCountedFailedLogin) -> BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey {
  BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey { account: bmc_counted_login_account(login: login), surface: bmc_counted_login_surface(login: login) }
}

// A RETRY THE PLAN DECLARES: how many further times it may present this
// account's credential on this surface, and why it believes it may need to
// (of: what it is retrying). extra_attempts is at least 1 because a retry that
// can never retry is not a retry, it is a restatement of the login beside it;
// and at most 32 because a plan that wants more has no budget question left —
// no controller this repository has evidence for serves a threshold that high.
// CONSUMER: BmcFailedLoginBudgetRequest.declared_retries, read by
// bmc_plan_failing_logins.
// HOW MANY TIMES A PLAN MAY PRESENT A CREDENTIAL AGAIN, bounded: at least once
// (a retry that can never retry is not a retry) and at most 32 (no controller this
// repository has evidence for serves a threshold that high, so a plan wanting more
// has no budget question left to ask). Named because a record field's constraint is
// fine but the same bound appears in two records and must say the same thing once.
type BmcDeclaredLoginExtraAttempts = Int where range(min: 1, max: 32)

type BmcDeclaredLoginRetry {
  account: NonEmptyStr
  surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface
  of: NonEmptyStr
  extra_attempts: BmcDeclaredLoginExtraAttempts
}

// ── THE ROSTER ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// How many potentially-failing logins a plan may make on one account+surface,
// with the plan's own list beside it in the order it makes them: a witness
// reads the count off the list, and an operator can see WHICH login is the one
// that would have locked the account.
type BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend {
  key: BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey
  logins: List<BmcCountedFailedLogin>
}

// A login the sealed forced-change state exempts, kept OUT of the spends so it
// can never be mistaken for a failure — and never quietly widened: attempts is
// how many logins this record exempts, and forced is the sealed record that
// says so, so a reader can walk from the exemption to the captured 403 behind
// it. See the section header for why the surface is checked.
type BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin {
  account: NonEmptyStr
  surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface
  attempts: BmcDeclaredLoginExtraAttempts
  forced: PublishedCredentialChangeForced
}

// The whole count of a plan: what it may spend, and what the sealed forced-change
// state says it may spend WITHOUT it counting.
type BmcPlanFailedLoginRoster {
  spends: List<BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend>
  exempt: List<BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin>
}

fn bmc_add_login(spends: List<BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend>, login: BmcCountedFailedLogin) -> List<BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend> {
  let key = bmc_counted_login_key(login: login)
  if any(spends, s => bmc_failed_login_budget_key_same(a: s.key, b: key)) {
    map(spends, s => if bmc_failed_login_budget_key_same(a: s.key, b: key) {
      BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend { key: s.key, logins: concat(s.logins, [login]) }
    } else { s })
  } else {
    concat(spends, [BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend { key: key, logins: [login] }])
  }
}

// Present the same credential again exactly n times: a declared retry of 3 costs
// 3 logins, not "up to 3, we lost track".
fn bmc_add_repeated_login(spends: List<BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend>, login: BmcCountedFailedLogin, times: Int) -> List<BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend> {
  if times <= 0 { spends } else { bmc_add_repeated_login(spends: bmc_add_login(spends: spends, login: login), login: login, times: times - 1) }
}

// TWO EXEMPTIONS ARE THE SAME EXEMPTION when they exempt the same account on the
// same surface under the same sealed build row: they merge into one record whose
// attempts add, so the roster cannot be padded with duplicate entries and a reader
// sees one number per account+surface.
fn bmc_exemption_matches(x: BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin, e: BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin) -> Bool {
  (x.account as String) == (e.account as String) && bmc_failed_login_surface_same(a: x.surface, b: e.surface) && bmc_credential_policy_key_eq(a: x.forced.key, b: e.forced.key)
}

fn bmc_add_exemption(exempt: List<BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin>, e: BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin) -> List<BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin> {
  if any(exempt, x => bmc_exemption_matches(x: x, e: e)) {
    map(exempt, x => if bmc_exemption_matches(x: x, e: e) { BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin { account: x.account, surface: x.surface, attempts: x.attempts + e.attempts, forced: x.forced } } else { x })
  } else {
    concat(exempt, [e])
  }
}

fn bmc_spend_count(spends: List<BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend>, key: BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey) -> Int {
  let hits = filter(spends, s => bmc_failed_login_budget_key_same(a: s.key, b: key))
  match list_head(hits) {
    Absent => 0
    Present { value: s } => list_length(s.logins)
  }
}

// The surface a planned write crosses, read off the route's own request. An
// IPMI Set User Password names no channel, so it is the undetermined arm; a
// privilege-limit write names the channel of the access row it sets.
fn bmc_write_surface(write: PlannedAccountWrite) -> BmcFailedLoginSurface {
  match grounded_request(standing: write.route) {
    Present { value: RedfishAccountPasswordWrite { account: _, transport_operation: _, action_shape: _ } } => RedfishAccountServiceLogin
    Present { value: IpmiSetUserPassword { user: _ } } => IpmiLanPlusLoginChannelUndetermined
    Present { value: IpmiSetUserPrivilegeLimit { access: a } } => IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: a.channel }
    Present { value: _ } => SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined
    Absent => SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined
  }
}

// Does the sealed forced-change state exempt a login on THIS surface? The carrier is
// `PublishedCredentialChangeForced`, which is SOLE-CONSTRUCTOR and mintable only by
// bmc_credential_policy.admit_published_credential_change_forced over a captured
// ForcedChangeResponseReading: a 403 whose bytes are the capture's, whose body the
// Redfish verdict reads as Base.1.16.0.PasswordChangeRequired, on a build the policy
// answers as forcing a factory change. There is no flag a caller can set to claim
// the exemption, and the record carries the identity of the answer it witnessed — so
// four conditions, each load-bearing:
//   - the SURFACE is Redfish: the sealed 403 body is a Redfish error body, and
//     bmc_credential_policy grounds the factory-login behaviour for that surface and
//     leaves the IPMI lanplus row ungrounded;
//   - the ENDPOINT is the one this plan's reading is of: a controller that was forced
//     does not make this controller forced;
//   - the ATTEMPT is the one this plan's reading was taken in: a 403 from an earlier
//     run does not license a login in this one, and a plan must rely on the answer it
//     actually received;
//   - the FIRMWARE is the one this reading reports: a forced change on 03.22.00 says
//     nothing about a controller that has since moved.
// CONSUMER: bmc_plan_failing_logins.
fn bmc_forced_change_covers(forced: PublishedCredentialChangeForced?, observed: BmcAccountStateObservation, surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface) -> PublishedCredentialChangeForced? {
  match forced {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: f } =>
      if !bmc_failed_login_surface_same(a: surface, b: RedfishAccountServiceLogin) {
        none
      } else if f.endpoint != observed.endpoint {
        // The 403 was read on a DIFFERENT controller. Its being forced says nothing
        // about logging into this one, so nothing is exempt here.
        none
      } else if f.attempt != observed.attempt {
        // And it was read in a DIFFERENT run of this controller. A forced answer
        // from an earlier attempt does not license a login in this one: the answer
        // the plan relies on has to be the answer this plan's reading received.
        none
      } else if !bmc_firmware_release_identity_eq(a: f.key.firmware, b: observed.firmware) {
        none
      } else {
        Present { value: f }
      }
  }
}

// THE WHOLE COUNT, from the plan's own parts. Every argument is a value the
// planner already holds; this adds no knowledge of its own, it only says, for
// each login the plan is allowed to make, whose counter it can move.
// CONSUMER: bmc_failed_login_budget_verdict, which plan_bmc_account_action runs.
fn bmc_plan_failing_logins(
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  observed: BmcAccountStateObservation,
  managed_write: PlannedAccountWrite?,
  published_write: PlannedPublishedWrite?,
  forced_change: PublishedCredentialChangeForced?,
  declared_retries: List<BmcDeclaredLoginRetry>,
) -> BmcPlanFailedLoginRoster {
  let managed_account = goal.managed.account
  let published_account = goal.published_break_glass.account
  let managed_surface = match managed_write {
    Present { value: w } => bmc_write_surface(write: w)
    Absent => SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined
  }
  let published_is_the_managed_write = match published_write {
    Present { value: PublishedWrittenSeparately { write: _ } } => false
    Present { value: PublishedIsTheManagedWrite } => true
    Absent => false
  }
  let published_surface = match published_write {
    Present { value: PublishedWrittenSeparately { write: w } } => bmc_write_surface(write: w)
    _ => managed_surface
  }
  // 1. THE MANAGED PROBE. The plan reads this account's state by logging in as
  //    it with the credential it believes is current, over the surface its
  //    managed write will use — the probe exists to say what that write needs.
  let after_managed = match managed_write {
    Present { value: _ } => bmc_add_login(spends: [], login: ManagedProbeLogin { account: managed_account, surface: managed_surface })
    Absent => []
  }
  // 2. THE BREAK-GLASS PROBE: its own login, on its own account's counter, made
  //    whenever the plan writes at all. When the published account IS the managed
  //    account it lands on the same counter as the managed probe, and it is STILL a
  //    second login: one stored password per account says at most one of the two
  //    presentations can be accepted, not that two presentations are one attempt.
  //    Only one authentication reused by both consumers would be one login, and the
  //    plan makes no such reuse (the reading's side of the same rule is
  //    bmc_break_glass_probe_is_the_managed_authentication).
  let after_break = match managed_write {
    Absent => after_managed
    Present { value: _ } => bmc_add_login(spends: after_managed, login: BreakGlassProbeLogin { account: published_account, surface: published_surface })
  }
  // 3. THE PUBLISHED PROBES: one login per addressed LAN member the published
  //    user may reach, charged to the PUBLISHED account on the channel each
  //    probe crossed. A derived (retired) published credential contributes
  //    NOTHING — that is the whole point of deriving it instead of probing it.
  let after_probes = match observed.published_credential {
    PublishedCredentialRetiredOnTheManagedAccount { derivation: _ } => after_break
    PublishedCredentialProbed { probes: probes } =>
      fold(probes, init: after_break, f: (acc, p) => {
        bmc_add_login(spends: acc, login: PublishedProbeLogin { account: published_account, surface: IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: p.channel }, channel: p.channel })
      })
  }
  // 4. THE PUBLISHED CREDENTIAL'S OWN AUTHENTICATION, when the plan retires it by
  //    writing the managed password over it: at that moment the plan holds only
  //    the published credential, so that login can be answered 401 and moves the
  //    published account's counter. The sealed forced-change state says the
  //    controller answers it with 403 PasswordChangeRequired instead —
  //    authenticated, not failed — so it is exempted AND RECORDED as exempt
  //    rather than dropped.
  let published_auth_login = if published_is_the_managed_write {
    Present { value: PublishedCredentialAuthenticationLogin { account: published_account, surface: managed_surface } }
  } else {
    none
  }
  let forced_covers_published_auth = match published_auth_login {
    Present { value: login } => bmc_forced_change_covers(forced: forced_change, observed: observed, surface: bmc_counted_login_surface(login: login))
    Absent => none
  }
  let spends_after_auth = match forced_covers_published_auth {
    Present { value: _ } => after_probes
    Absent => match published_auth_login {
      Present { value: login } => bmc_add_login(spends: after_probes, login: login)
      Absent => after_probes
    }
  }
  let exempt_after_auth = match forced_covers_published_auth {
    Present { value: f } => bmc_add_exemption([], e: BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin { account: published_account, surface: managed_surface, attempts: 1, forced: f })
    Absent => []
  }
  // 5. DECLARED RETRIES: each further presentation the plan declares is another
  //    login the controller may count as a failure on that account+surface.
  fold(declared_retries, init: BmcPlanFailedLoginRoster { spends: spends_after_auth, exempt: exempt_after_auth }, f: (acc, r) => {
    BmcPlanFailedLoginRoster {
      spends: bmc_add_repeated_login(spends: acc.spends, login: DeclaredRetryLogin { account: r.account, surface: r.surface, of: r.of }, times: r.extra_attempts),
      exempt: acc.exempt,
    }
  })
}

// ── THE SERVED LOCKOUT READING ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// The controller's own answer, kept per surface, beside the other account
// readings. Nothing here is a default: LockoutPolicyNotReadable is a state of the
// controller (on OpenBMC 03.22.00 NOTHING authenticated is readable before the
// forced change — every authenticated GET is answered 403
// Base.1.16.0.PasswordChangeRequired, which is exactly what
// artifacts/bmc/srv13-first-contact-2026-10-07/bmc-3.22.00-factory-login-403.json
// records), and §5 forbids turning "we could not read it" into a number.

// Where a surface's policy came from. The two arms carry the extdeps shapes
// verbatim, so a reader can walk from a refusal to the served properties that
// produced it.
type BmcServedLockoutSource =
    ServedFromRedfishAccountService { properties: RedfishAccountServiceLockoutServed }
  | ServedFromIpmiLanBadPasswordThreshold { parameters: IpmiLanBadPasswordThreshold }

// WHY a surface's served policy could not be read. Each arm is a different
// controller behaviour, and they are not interchangeable for the operator: the
// first says the controller will not answer until the forced change happens
// (nothing to do but use the forced-change path), the second says it answered
// with an error to an authenticated read, the third says this controller simply
// has no such parameter (a real state of some firmware: no threshold is served,
// so no number may be invented), the fourth says the read itself failed.
type BmcLockoutNotReadableCause =
    NothingAuthenticatedBeforeTheForcedChange { forced: PublishedCredentialChangeForced }
  | ControllerRefusedTheAuthenticatedRead { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | ControllerServesNoLockoutParameter { detail: NonEmptyStr }
  | LockoutReadAttemptFailed { detail: NonEmptyStr }

type BmcServedLockoutPolicy =
    LockoutPolicyServed { served: BmcServedLockoutSource }
  | LockoutPolicyNotReadable { cause: BmcLockoutNotReadableCause }

type BmcLockoutSurfaceReading sole_constructor {
  surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface
  policy: BmcServedLockoutPolicy
  evidence: EvidenceRef
  // WHEN THIS SURFACE WAS READ, on the observer clock. Part of the reading's
  // identity, so a plan cannot be admitted against a threshold the controller may
  // since have been told to change.
  read_at: ObserverClockInstant
}

// THE PER-CONTROLLER LOCKOUT READING, carried by BmcAccountStateObservation
// beside the census and the probes. read_at is the observer instant the reads
// were taken, so the read-floor rule that governs every other reading in the
// observation governs this one too.
//
// WHY IT IS NOT A PER-BUILD ROW (design settled in
// gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_credential_policy's module comment): the threshold is
// a property the controller SERVES and an operator can change — an
// AccountService PATCH, a Set LAN Configuration Parameters on the H11SSL units —
// so a row keyed by board and firmware would go stale the moment that happens,
// and a stale threshold is precisely how a rotation locks the account it is
// meant to protect.
type BmcControllerLockoutReading sole_constructor {
  read_at: ObserverClockInstant
  surfaces: List<BmcLockoutSurfaceReading>
}

// THE ADAPTERS: controller verdict → this fold's reading. They add no numbers;
// they only place the served properties where the budget can use them, and turn
// a not-readable verdict into the typed cause rather than an absence.

// not_authenticated is WHAT THE READER KNOWS about the refusal, and it is the
// reader's to know: the 403 Base.1.16.0.PasswordChangeRequired case is only
// something the reader can say, because it is the sealed
// PublishedCredentialChangeForced of the build it read — the extdeps verdict
// carries an HTTP status, which is not an exemption. A caller that cannot seal a
// forced change passes ControllerRefusedTheAuthenticatedRead, and the budget then
// refuses instead of assuming the 403.
fn bmc_lockout_surface_from_redfish(
  verdict: RedfishAccountServiceLockoutVerdict,
  not_authenticated: BmcLockoutNotReadableCause,
  evidence: EvidenceRef,
  read_at: ObserverClockInstant,
) -> BmcLockoutSurfaceReading {
  BmcLockoutSurfaceReading {
    surface: RedfishAccountServiceLogin,
    policy: match verdict {
      RedfishAccountServiceLockoutPropertiesRead { served: s } => LockoutPolicyServed { served: ServedFromRedfishAccountService { properties: s } }
      RedfishAccountServiceLockoutPropertiesNotAuthenticated { http_status: _, detail: _ } => LockoutPolicyNotReadable { cause: not_authenticated }
      RedfishAccountServiceLockoutPropertiesUnreadable { detail: d } => LockoutPolicyNotReadable { cause: LockoutReadAttemptFailed { detail: d } }
    },
    evidence: evidence,
    read_at: read_at,
  }
}

fn bmc_lockout_surface_from_ipmi_lan(verdict: IpmiLanBadPasswordThresholdVerdict, evidence: EvidenceRef, read_at: ObserverClockInstant) -> BmcLockoutSurfaceReading {
  match verdict {
    IpmiLanBadPasswordThresholdRead { channel: c, served: s } => BmcLockoutSurfaceReading {
      surface: IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: c },
      policy: LockoutPolicyServed { served: ServedFromIpmiLanBadPasswordThreshold { parameters: s } },
      evidence: evidence,
      read_at: read_at,
    }
    IpmiLanBadPasswordThresholdNotAvailable { channel: c } => BmcLockoutSurfaceReading {
      surface: IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: c },
      policy: LockoutPolicyNotReadable { cause: ControllerServesNoLockoutParameter { detail: ipmi_lan_channel_text(channel: c) } },
      evidence: evidence,
      read_at: read_at,
    }
    IpmiLanBadPasswordThresholdReadFailed { channel: c, detail: d } => BmcLockoutSurfaceReading {
      surface: IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: c },
      policy: LockoutPolicyNotReadable { cause: LockoutReadAttemptFailed { detail: join([ipmi_lan_channel_text(channel: c), ": ", d], "") } },
      evidence: evidence,
      read_at: read_at,
    }
  }
}

fn ipmi_lan_channel_text(channel: IpmiChannelNumber) -> NonEmptyStr {
  join(["IPMI LAN channel ", to_string(channel as Int)], "")
}

// THE ONLY WAY TO HOLD ONE OF THESE OUTSIDE THIS MODULE (the record is
// sole_constructor): a reader places each surface's served policy here, with the
// receipt of the read that produced it.
// CONSUMER: bmc_lockout_surface_from_redfish, bmc_lockout_surface_from_ipmi_lan,
// bmc_lockout_reading_not_read, and test.fixture.machine_intake.bmc_lockout.
fn bmc_lockout_surface(surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface, policy: BmcServedLockoutPolicy, evidence: EvidenceRef, read_at: ObserverClockInstant) -> BmcLockoutSurfaceReading {
  BmcLockoutSurfaceReading { surface: surface, policy: policy, evidence: evidence, read_at: read_at }
}

fn bmc_lockout_reading(surfaces: List<BmcLockoutSurfaceReading>, read_at: ObserverClockInstant) -> BmcControllerLockoutReading {
  BmcControllerLockoutReading { read_at: read_at, surfaces: surfaces }
}

// THE THRESHOLD FOR A SURFACE, in the fold's own vocabulary. WHY A THIRD STATE
// BEYOND SERVED/NOT-SERVED: "never locked out" and "we could not read it" are
// both controller states but they license opposite plans, so they are never
// collapsed — and neither is ever taken from an absent property (the extdeps
// shapes hold Option for exactly this reason; the reading turns an absent
// threshold into LockoutThresholdUnread, never into 0).
// A served threshold that locks the account: BOTH upstream sources bound it on both
// sides, and the bound is carried rather than re-derived here — AccountService.v1_19_0
// AccountLockoutThreshold is a UInt32 whose 0 means "never locked" (that arm is
// AccountNeverLockedOutByThisController, so a value reaching this one is >= 1), and
// the IPMI LAN Bad Password Threshold byte is 1..255 (ipmitool's
// IPMI_LANP_BAD_PASS_THRESH). The product bound is therefore the union of the two
// upstream bounds, min 1 to max the UInt32 ceiling. Derived counts (how many failures
// fall in a window, how many a plan may still make) are plain Ints: they are computed
// here, not served upstream, and clamping them is this module's own arithmetic.
type BmcAccountLockoutFailedAttempts = Int where range(min: 1, max: 4294967295)

type BmcLockoutThreshold =
    AccountNeverLockedOutByThisController { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | AccountLockedOutAfter { failed_attempts: BmcAccountLockoutFailedAttempts }
  | LockoutThresholdUnread { cause: NonEmptyStr }

// The threshold whose REFUSAL the plan must fit, per surface. The two upstream
// rules are taken from the served shapes, not inferred here:
//   - Redfish: AccountLockoutThreshold == 0 means the account shall never be
//     locked (AccountService.v1_19_0), via
//     redfish_account_lockout_threshold_locks_after.
//   - IPMI: invalid_password_disable false means the bad-password threshold is
//     not in force, via ipmi_lan_bad_password_threshold_locks_after.
// NOTE, and it is deliberate: AccountLockoutDuration == 0 does NOT exempt a
// plan. The schema says no lockout "shall occur" when it is 0, but it also says
// the duration is ignored when AccountLockoutCounterResetEnabled is false, and a
// controller whose reset is disabled keeps the account locked until an
// administrator resets it — so treating a 0 duration as free passage would
// license a plan against the one configuration where a lockout is most
// expensive. Being refused for a plan that could not have been locked is the
// safe direction; locking out the only administrator is not.
fn bmc_lockout_threshold(surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface, reading: BmcControllerLockoutReading) -> BmcLockoutThreshold {
  let found = filter(reading.surfaces, s => bmc_failed_login_surface_same(a: s.surface, b: surface))
  match list_head(found) {
    // No entry for this surface means it was never read on this controller. Fail
    // closed: an unread surface licenses no login, exactly as an unread threshold
    // does on a surface that was read.
    Absent => LockoutThresholdUnread { cause: join(["no lockout reading was taken for ", bmc_failed_login_surface_text(surface: surface)], "") }
    Present { value: entry } => match entry.policy {
      LockoutPolicyNotReadable { cause: c } => LockoutThresholdUnread { cause: bmc_lockout_not_readable_text(cause: c, surface: surface) }
      LockoutPolicyServed { served: ServedFromRedfishAccountService { properties: p } } =>
        match redfish_account_lockout_threshold_locks_after(served: p) {
          AccountIsNeverLockedByServedThreshold => AccountNeverLockedOutByThisController { reason: "AccountService.AccountLockoutThreshold is 0: the controller serves no lockout on this account (AccountService.v1_19_0)" }
          AccountLocksAfter { failed_attempts: n } => AccountLockedOutAfter { failed_attempts: n as Int }
        }
      LockoutPolicyServed { served: ServedFromIpmiLanBadPasswordThreshold { parameters: p } } =>
        match entry.surface {
          // The channel comes from the entry's own surface, never from a default:
          // a served IPMI reading is keyed by the channel it was read on.
          IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: c } => match ipmi_lan_bad_password_threshold_locks_after(channel: c, served: p) {
            IpmiLanUsersAreNotLockedOut { reason: r } => AccountNeverLockedOutByThisController { reason: r }
            IpmiLanLocksAfter { failed_attempts: n } => AccountLockedOutAfter { failed_attempts: n as Int }
          }
          _ => LockoutThresholdUnread { cause: join(["an IPMI LAN lockout reading is carried on a non-IPMI surface: ", bmc_failed_login_surface_text(surface: surface)], "") }
        }
    }
  }
}

// ── THE COUNTERS A LOGIN CAN MOVE ────────────────────────────────────────────
// The controller keeps one failed-attempt counter per account on each surface it
// serves a policy for: the Redfish AccountService, and each IPMI LAN channel. A
// login the plan names lands on exactly one of them. A login it cannot name -- an
// IPMI login whose channel the lanplus transport picks, or a write whose request
// names no surface -- may land on ANY counter it can reach, and the plan does not
// get to choose after the fact, so it is charged to EVERY one of them, BESIDE
// whatever else that counter is already charged with and whatever it has already
// counted. Judging it as a separate pseudo-counter against the tightest threshold
// undercounts twice: two undetermined logins and one named to channel 1 each fit a
// headroom of 2 on their own while all three can reach channel 1, and a failure
// already on channel 1 never reduced the undetermined login's headroom.
//
// AND A PARTIAL READING BOUNDS NOTHING. A login of unknown transport could land on
// the Redfish counter or on any LAN channel's; spending it against only the
// transport that happened to be read treats the unread one as if it did not exist,
// the fabrication this gate exists to prevent. So the unnamed-write arm needs both
// transports read (a Redfish AccountService surface and at least one LAN channel),
// and the unnamed-channel arm at least one LAN channel; otherwise the login is not
// bounded and refuses. Today plan_bmc_account_action cannot reach the unnamed-write
// arm -- the write admissions refuse a route with no named request first -- so it
// is witnessed at function level for the day a plan mints such a write.
type BmcCountersReached =
    CountersReached { surfaces: List<BmcFailedLoginSurface> }
  | CountersNotBounded { cause: NonEmptyStr }

fn bmc_counters_reached(surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface, reading: BmcControllerLockoutReading) -> BmcCountersReached {
  let channels = map(filter(reading.surfaces, s => match s.surface { IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: _ } => true, _ => false }), s => s.surface)
  match surface {
    RedfishAccountServiceLogin => CountersReached { surfaces: [surface] }
    IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: _ } => CountersReached { surfaces: [surface] }
    IpmiLanPlusLoginChannelUndetermined =>
      if list_length(channels) == 0 {
        CountersNotBounded { cause: "no IPMI LAN channel of this controller was read, so the channel the lanplus transport will address is unknown" }
      } else {
        CountersReached { surfaces: channels }
      }
    SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined => {
      let saw_redfish = list_length(filter(reading.surfaces, s => match s.surface { RedfishAccountServiceLogin => true, _ => false })) > 0
      if !(saw_redfish && list_length(channels) > 0) {
        CountersNotBounded { cause: "this login's surface is not named by the plan and the reading did not cover every transport it could authenticate on — the Redfish AccountService policy and a LAN channel policy are both needed to bound it" }
      } else {
        CountersReached { surfaces: concat([RedfishAccountServiceLogin], channels) }
      }
    }
  }
}

// Can a login (or a recorded failure) on `from` have moved the concrete counter
// `counter`? An unbounded surface can have moved any of them.
fn bmc_surface_reaches_counter(from: BmcFailedLoginSurface, counter: BmcFailedLoginSurface, reading: BmcControllerLockoutReading) -> Bool {
  match bmc_counters_reached(surface: from, reading: reading) {
    CountersReached { surfaces: ss } => any(ss, s => bmc_failed_login_surface_same(a: s, b: counter))
    CountersNotBounded { cause: _ } => true
  }
}

fn bmc_failed_login_surface_text(surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match surface {
    RedfishAccountServiceLogin => "Redfish AccountService"
    IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: c } => ipmi_lan_channel_text(channel: c)
    IpmiLanPlusLoginChannelUndetermined => "IPMI LAN (channel chosen by the transport)"
    SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined => "the surface of a write whose route carries no request"
  }
}

fn bmc_lockout_not_readable_text(cause: BmcLockoutNotReadableCause, surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match cause {
    NothingAuthenticatedBeforeTheForcedChange { forced: f } => join([bmc_failed_login_surface_text(surface: surface), ": nothing authenticated is readable before the forced change (", f.message_id, " on firmware ", f.key.firmware.raw_version, ")"], "")
    ControllerRefusedTheAuthenticatedRead { detail: d } => join([bmc_failed_login_surface_text(surface: surface), ": the controller refused the authenticated read (", d, ")"], "")
    ControllerServesNoLockoutParameter { detail: d } => join([bmc_failed_login_surface_text(surface: surface), ": the controller serves no lockout parameter (", d, ")"], "")
    LockoutReadAttemptFailed { detail: d } => join([bmc_failed_login_surface_text(surface: surface), ": the lockout read failed (", d, ")"], "")
  }
}

// THE RESET WINDOW: how long a failed attempt keeps counting. Not the plan's
// choice and not a constant — Redfish serves AccountLockoutCounterResetAfter
// (seconds, from the last failed attempt; the counter also resets on a
// SUCCESSFUL login) and AccountLockoutCounterResetEnabled, whose schema default
// when the property is absent is TRUE; IPMI serves attempt_count_reset_secs in
// the same block as the threshold. Absent means UNREAD, not infinite, and never
// a borrowed 300 from the H11SSL capture.
type BmcFailedAttemptWindow =
    // The window as the repo's own time unit, produced at the extdeps boundary
    // (redfish_account_lockout_counter_reset_window, ipmi_lan_attempt_count_reset_window).
    // No layer below this one multiplies it by a factor to compare with a timestamp.
    FailedAttemptsCountedFor { window: Second }
  | FailedAttemptsNeverReset { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | FailedAttemptWindowUnread { detail: NonEmptyStr }

fn bmc_failed_attempt_window(surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface, reading: BmcControllerLockoutReading) -> BmcFailedAttemptWindow {
  let found = filter(reading.surfaces, s => bmc_failed_login_surface_same(a: s.surface, b: surface))
  match list_head(found) {
    Absent => FailedAttemptWindowUnread { detail: join(["no lockout reading was taken for ", bmc_failed_login_surface_text(surface: surface)], "") }
    Present { value: entry } => match entry.policy {
      LockoutPolicyNotReadable { cause: c } => FailedAttemptWindowUnread { detail: bmc_lockout_not_readable_text(cause: c, surface: surface) }
      LockoutPolicyServed { served: ServedFromRedfishAccountService { properties: p } } =>
        // With counter-reset disabled a locked account stays locked until an
        // administrator resets it, so the window is unbounded: any failure the
        // operator cannot show to be old still counts.
        if !redfish_account_lockout_counter_reset_enabled_reads(served: p) {
          FailedAttemptsNeverReset { reason: "AccountService.AccountLockoutCounterResetEnabled is false: the account stays locked until an administrator resets it (AccountService.v1_19_0)" }
        } else {
          // The seconds this property serves become a time measure at the
          // extdeps boundary (redfish_account_lockout_counter_reset_window), so this
          // layer never holds a bare count of them and never scales one itself. An
          // absent property stays Absent here and is reported as an unread window.
          match redfish_account_lockout_counter_reset_window(served: p) {
            Present { value: w } => FailedAttemptsCountedFor { window: w }
            Absent => FailedAttemptWindowUnread { detail: join([bmc_failed_login_surface_text(surface: surface), ": AccountService.AccountLockoutCounterResetAfter is not served"], "") }
          }
        }
      LockoutPolicyServed { served: ServedFromIpmiLanBadPasswordThreshold { parameters: p } } =>
        if !ipmi_lan_failed_attempts_drive_lockout(served: p) {
          FailedAttemptsNeverReset { reason: join([bmc_failed_login_surface_text(surface: surface), ": invalid password disable is off, so a lockout on this channel is not driven by the failed-attempt counter at all"], "") }
        } else {
          FailedAttemptsCountedFor { window: ipmi_lan_attempt_count_reset_window(served: p) }
        }
    }
  }
}

// A FAILED ATTEMPT THE READING ALREADY KNOWS ABOUT, so the budget counts against
// what is left rather than against the full threshold. at is the observer instant
// the rejection was recorded; a rejection whose surface the plan does not use is
// not this key's business and is never silently dropped — the caller passes one
// entry per (account, surface) it observed a rejection on.
type BmcKnownFailedLogin {
  key: BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey
  at: EpochMs
}

fn bmc_known_failed_login(account: NonEmptyStr, surface: BmcFailedLoginSurface, at: EpochMs) -> BmcKnownFailedLogin {
  BmcKnownFailedLogin { key: BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey { account: account, surface: surface }, at: at }
}

// HOW MANY OF THE KNOWN FAILURES ARE STILL ON THIS COUNTER. Every recorded failure
// of the account on a surface that can reach the counter is a candidate (see
// bmc_surface_reaches_counter). An unread or unbounded window counts every one of
// them -- section 5, fail closed: the operator cannot show a failure to be old.
fn bmc_known_failures_in_window(known: List<BmcKnownFailedLogin>, key: BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey, window: BmcFailedAttemptWindow, now: EpochMs, reading: BmcControllerLockoutReading) -> Int {
  let mine = filter(known, k => (k.key.account as String) == (key.account as String) && bmc_surface_reaches_counter(from: k.key.surface, counter: key.surface, reading: reading))
  match window {
    FailedAttemptsNeverReset { reason: _ } => list_length(mine)
    FailedAttemptWindowUnread { detail: _ } => list_length(mine)
    FailedAttemptsCountedFor { window: window } => {
      // The measure converts itself: seconds to milliseconds is
      // second_to_millisecond, and the elapsed value it is compared with is already
      // a millisecond difference of EpochMs. There is no local factor here because
      // there is no local unit.
      let window_ms: Int = millisecond_count(m: second_to_millisecond(s: window))
      // A served window of 0 seconds is NOT read as "nothing counts": upstream
      // gives no sentence that licenses dropping a failure the controller has
      // already counted, so a 0 window counts everything too.
      if window_ms <= 0 { list_length(mine) } else { bmc_failures_since_the_last_quiet_interval(failures: mine, window_ms: window_ms, now: now) }
    }
  }
}

// THE COUNTER IS RESET BY A QUIET INTERVAL, NOT BY EACH FAILURE AGEING OUT.
// AccountService.AccountLockoutCounterResetAfter is the interval from the LAST
// failed login until the counter returns to zero (AccountService.v1_19_0), so a
// failure stays counted for as long as later failures keep the counter active:
// threshold 3, window 300 s, failures at T and T+290, evaluated at T+310 -- no
// 300 s has passed without a failure, the counter holds 2, and expiring the first
// failure on its own age would report 1 and admit the login that locks the account.
// The walk goes from `now` back through the failures, newest first: each failure no
// further than the window from the one after it (or from `now`) is still counted,
// and the first gap longer than the window is the reset, behind which nothing
// counts. A failure stamped after `now` (an observer clock that skewed between the
// rejection and the plan) cannot be shown to be old and is counted without moving
// the walk. A SUCCESSFUL login also resets the Redfish counter, and no reading here
// records one, so this count is never below the controller's. The IPMI LAN
// attempt-count reset is read the same way: of the readings of "reset after the
// interval" this is the one that counts the most, so it holds whichever the
// controller implements.
type BmcCounterWalk {
  since: Int
  counted: Int
  reset: Bool
}

fn bmc_failures_since_the_last_quiet_interval(failures: List<BmcKnownFailedLogin>, window_ms: Int, now: EpochMs) -> Int {
  // Newest first: the sort is ascending on the negated instant, and it is stable.
  let newest_first = list_sort_by_key(xs: failures, key: k => 0 - (k.at as Int), order: int_total_order())
  let walked = fold(newest_first, init: BmcCounterWalk { since: now as Int, counted: 0, reset: false }, f: (w, k) => {
    if w.reset {
      w
    } else if (k.at as Int) > (now as Int) {
      BmcCounterWalk { since: w.since, counted: w.counted + 1, reset: false }
    } else if w.since - (k.at as Int) <= window_ms {
      BmcCounterWalk { since: k.at as Int, counted: w.counted + 1, reset: false }
    } else {
      BmcCounterWalk { since: w.since, counted: w.counted, reset: true }
    }
  })
  walked.counted
}

// ── THE HEADROOM AND THE VERDICT ─────────────────────────────────────────────
type BmcFailedLoginHeadroom =
    AccountNotLockedOutByThisController { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | HeadroomKnown { threshold: BmcAccountLockoutFailedAttempts, known_failures_in_window: Int, may_fail: Int }
  | HeadroomUnknown { cause: NonEmptyStr }

// The headroom of ONE CONCRETE COUNTER: the key's surface is the Redfish
// AccountService or one IPMI LAN channel, never an undetermined surface (those are
// spread onto the counters they reach before the gate asks).
fn bmc_failed_login_headroom(key: BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey, reading: BmcControllerLockoutReading, known: List<BmcKnownFailedLogin>, now: EpochMs) -> BmcFailedLoginHeadroom {
  match bmc_lockout_threshold(surface: key.surface, reading: reading) {
    AccountNeverLockedOutByThisController { reason: r } => AccountNotLockedOutByThisController { reason: r }
    LockoutThresholdUnread { cause: c } => HeadroomUnknown { cause: c }
    AccountLockedOutAfter { failed_attempts: n } => {
      let window = bmc_failed_attempt_window(surface: key.surface, reading: reading)
      let used = bmc_known_failures_in_window(known: known, key: key, window: window, now: now, reading: reading)
      let room = (n as Int) - 1 - used
      HeadroomKnown { threshold: n, known_failures_in_window: used, may_fail: if room < 0 { 0 } else { room } }
    }
  }
}

// WHY A PLAN'S LOGIN COUNT IS REFUSED, in the two shapes that are genuinely
// different: MORE THAN THE CONTROLLER LEAVES (the operator can shrink the plan,
// or reset the counter and re-read) versus NO SERVED THRESHOLD TO PLAN AGAINST
// (the operator has to read the policy first, or produce the sealed forced-change
// state). Collapsing them would tell an operator to shrink a plan that was
// already small enough.
type BmcFailedLoginBudgetBlock
  = CostExceedsTheServedHeadroom { cost: Int, may_fail: Int, threshold: BmcAccountLockoutFailedAttempts, known_failures_in_window: Int }
  | FailingLoginsWithNoServedThreshold { cost: Int, cause: NonEmptyStr }

type BmcFailedLoginBudgetBlockReading {
  key: BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey
  block: BmcFailedLoginBudgetBlock
}

type BmcFailedLoginBudgetVerdict
  = FailedLoginBudgetAdmitted { spends: List<BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend>, exempt: List<BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin> }
  | FailedLoginBudgetRefused { blocked: List<BmcFailedLoginBudgetBlockReading>, spends: List<BmcPlanFailedLoginSpend>, exempt: List<BmcForcedChangeExemptLogin> }

// THE GATE. plan_bmc_account_action runs this before it mints anything: the
// refusal is produced at PLAN time, so no write is asked for and no approval is
// spent. It judges every CONCRETE COUNTER a spend can reach, charging that counter
// with every spend of the same account that can reach it -- named or not -- and
// with every recorded failure that can have moved it, and it refuses the whole
// plan if any one counter is over. A spend whose counters cannot be bounded
// refuses on its own key.
fn bmc_failed_login_budget_verdict(
  roster: BmcPlanFailedLoginRoster,
  reading: BmcControllerLockoutReading,
  known: List<BmcKnownFailedLogin>,
  now: EpochMs,
) -> BmcFailedLoginBudgetVerdict {
  let unbounded: List<BmcFailedLoginBudgetBlockReading> = fold(roster.spends, init: [], f: (acc, s) => {
    let cost = list_length(s.logins)
    match bmc_counters_reached(surface: s.key.surface, reading: reading) {
      CountersReached { surfaces: _ } => acc
      // A spend recorded with zero logins is not a login and refuses nothing.
      CountersNotBounded { cause: c } => if cost > 0 {
        concat(acc, [BmcFailedLoginBudgetBlockReading { key: s.key, block: FailingLoginsWithNoServedThreshold { cost: cost, cause: c } }])
      } else { acc }
    }
  })
  let counters: List<BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey> = fold(roster.spends, init: [], f: (acc, s) => match bmc_counters_reached(surface: s.key.surface, reading: reading) {
    CountersNotBounded { cause: _ } => acc
    CountersReached { surfaces: ss } => fold(ss, init: acc, f: (a, surface) => {
      let k = BmcFailedLoginBudgetKey { account: s.key.account, surface: surface }
      if any(a, x => bmc_failed_login_budget_key_same(a: x, b: k)) { a } else { concat(a, [k]) }
    })
  })
  let over: List<BmcFailedLoginBudgetBlockReading> = fold(counters, init: [], f: (acc, k) => {
    let cost = fold(roster.spends, init: 0, f: (n, s) =>
      if (s.key.account as String) == (k.account as String) && bmc_surface_reaches_counter(from: s.key.surface, counter: k.surface, reading: reading) {
        n + list_length(s.logins)
      } else { n })
    match bmc_failed_login_headroom(key: k, reading: reading, known: known, now: now) {
      // The controller serves no lockout on this account+surface: nothing this
      // plan does here can lock it, whatever the count.
      AccountNotLockedOutByThisController { reason: _ } => acc
      HeadroomKnown { threshold: t, known_failures_in_window: used, may_fail: may } =>
        if cost > may {
          concat(acc, [BmcFailedLoginBudgetBlockReading { key: k, block: CostExceedsTheServedHeadroom { cost: cost, may_fail: may, threshold: t, known_failures_in_window: used } }])
        } else {
          acc
        }
      // No threshold means no headroom can be computed, so ONE potentially-failing
      // login is enough to refuse.
      HeadroomUnknown { cause: c } =>
        if cost > 0 {
          concat(acc, [BmcFailedLoginBudgetBlockReading { key: k, block: FailingLoginsWithNoServedThreshold { cost: cost, cause: c } }])
        } else {
          acc
        }
    }
  })
  let blocked = concat(unbounded, over)
  if list_length(blocked) > 0 {
    FailedLoginBudgetRefused { blocked: blocked, spends: roster.spends, exempt: roster.exempt }
  } else {
    FailedLoginBudgetAdmitted { spends: roster.spends, exempt: roster.exempt }
  }
}

// THE FRONTIERS.
//
// The live read is not wired in this change (the brief: live reads are out of
// scope), so nothing here asserts what any controller in the fleet serves. When
// the read lands, it lands as the two extdeps verdict shapes above — a Redfish
// GET of AccountService and a Get LAN Configuration Parameters on the addressed
// channel — through the two adapters, and the witnesses below are replaced by
// receipts. NOT satisfied by a capture under artifacts/bmc/ standing in for a
// read: the H11SSL "Bad Password Threshold : 3" is a REPORTED read of one unit at
// one moment, and the threshold is operator-writable.
data bmc_served_lockout_live_read_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "dissolves when the account-state read of gunbc.machine_intake.bmc_secure takes its BmcControllerLockoutReading from a live Redfish GET of AccountService (extdeps.bmc.redfish RedfishAccountServiceLockoutVerdict) and a live Get LAN Configuration Parameters of the addressed channel (extdeps.bmc.ipmi_channel IpmiLanBadPasswordThresholdVerdict), through bmc_lockout_surface_from_redfish and bmc_lockout_surface_from_ipmi_lan, on a controller this repository holds a subject for; NOT satisfied by a witness passing a forged reading, by the H11SSL lan-print capture, or by any per-build row" as NonEmptyStr,
)

// THE ONE EXCLUSION THIS SECTION MAKES, said out loud instead of left silent.
// A plan's WRITE authentication is not counted as a potentially-failing login:
// its authorization is checked before the request is built
// (ScopedAuthorization<BmcAccountWriteApproval>, read_bmc_write_approval), and by
// the time the write runs the same credential has just been ACCEPTED by the
// probe beside it on the same account — a credential accepted seconds ago is not
// a failing login. If that stops holding — if a realization authenticates a write
// with a credential it has NOT just had accepted, or retries the write after a
// rejection — this exclusion is wrong and every plan that relies on it is
// under-counted.
data bmc_write_authentication_failed_login_frontier: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(
  description: "dissolves when any realization of a BmcAccountActionPlan authenticates a password write with a credential it has not just had ACCEPTED on the same account and surface in the same plan (a write retried after a 401, or a write issued without the managed probe preceding it); at that point the write's authentication must be counted as a potentially-failing login in bmc_plan_failing_logins" as NonEmptyStr,
)

// ONE AUTHENTICATION OR TWO. The break-glass probe is the managed probe's own
// authentication only when it IS that reading: the same evidence (label and digest)
// observed at the same instant. Two probes that present the same account, even the
// same password, are two authentications with two pieces of evidence, and the dry
// reader takes two (its "managed" and "break-glass" probes). An unestablished probe
// made no recorded authentication and is never the same event as anything.
// CONSUMER: bmc_known_failed_logins_of.
fn bmc_break_glass_probe_is_the_managed_authentication(managed: ObservedCredentialProbe, break_glass: ObservedCredentialProbe) -> Bool {
  match bmc_probe_recorded_reading(probe: managed) {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: a } => match bmc_probe_recorded_reading(probe: break_glass) {
      Absent => false
      Present { value: b } =>
        bmc_probe_accepted(probe: managed) == bmc_probe_accepted(probe: break_glass)
          && (observer_instant_millis(instant: a.observed_at) as Int) == (observer_instant_millis(instant: b.observed_at) as Int)
          && a.evidence.label == b.evidence.label
          && content_hash_equal(left: a.evidence.digest, right: b.evidence.digest)
    }
  }
}

fn bmc_probe_recorded_reading(probe: ObservedCredentialProbe) -> ObservedReading? {
  match probe {
    ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: r } => Present { value: r }
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: r } => Present { value: r }
    ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: _ } => none
  }
}

fn bmc_probe_accepted(probe: ObservedCredentialProbe) -> Bool {
  match probe {
    ObservedCredentialAccepted { reading: _ } => true
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: _ } => false
    ObservedCredentialUnestablished { detail: _ } => false
  }
}

// THE FAILURES THE READING ALREADY KNOWS ABOUT. The budget counts against what is
// LEFT, not against the full threshold, so a controller that has already rejected
// two of three attempts must not be promised a third. A rejection is attributed to
// the account it authenticated as and the surface it crossed — the same key the
// roster charges the planned login to, so a rejection of the managed probe is
// charged against the plan's own managed probe and nothing else.
//
// THE BREAK-GLASS REJECTION IS ITS OWN FAILURE unless it is the managed probe's own
// authentication read twice. Sharing an account, or one stored password per account,
// does not make two presentations of a password one attempt: threshold 4 with two
// distinct rejections leaves 4 - 1 - 2 = 1, and folding them into one would promise
// 2. The deduplication rests on the identity of the authentication event and on
// nothing about the account (bmc_break_glass_probe_is_the_managed_authentication).
fn bmc_known_failed_logins_of(
  observed: BmcAccountStateObservation,
  goal: BmcSecureGoal,
  managed_write: PlannedAccountWrite?,
  published_write: PlannedPublishedWrite?,
) -> List<BmcKnownFailedLogin> {
  let managed_surface = match managed_write {
    Present { value: w } => bmc_write_surface(write: w)
    Absent => SurfaceOfThePlannedWriteUndetermined
  }
  let published_surface = match published_write {
    Present { value: PublishedWrittenSeparately { write: w } } => bmc_write_surface(write: w)
    _ => managed_surface
  }
  let managed_rejected = match observed.managed_probe {
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: r } => [bmc_known_failed_login(account: goal.managed.account, surface: managed_surface, at: observer_instant_millis(instant: r.observed_at))]
    _ => []
  }
  let break_rejected = match observed.break_glass_probe {
    ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: r } =>
      if bmc_break_glass_probe_is_the_managed_authentication(managed: observed.managed_probe, break_glass: observed.break_glass_probe) {
        []
      } else {
        [bmc_known_failed_login(account: goal.published_break_glass.account, surface: published_surface, at: observer_instant_millis(instant: r.observed_at))]
      }
    _ => []
  }
  let probe_rejected = match observed.published_credential {
    PublishedCredentialRetiredOnTheManagedAccount { derivation: _ } => []
    PublishedCredentialProbed { probes: probes } => fold(probes, init: [], f: (acc, p) => {
      match p.probe {
        ObservedCredentialRejected { reading: r } => concat(acc, [bmc_known_failed_login(account: goal.published_break_glass.account, surface: IpmiLanPlusLogin { channel: p.channel }, at: observer_instant_millis(instant: r.observed_at))])
        _ => acc
      }
    })
  }
  concat(concat(managed_rejected, break_rejected), probe_rejected)
}

// A READER THAT COULD NOT READ SAYS SO. This is the honest input for a pass that
// took no lockout read — including today's dry reader, which reads none: every
// surface it reports is NotReadable with the reason the caller gives, and the
// budget gate then refuses any plan carrying a potentially-failing login. It takes
// no threshold, no window and no channel from anywhere, so there is no number here
// for a plan to lean on (§5).
// CONSUMER: callers of dry_read_bmc_account_state and any reader that has no
// AccountService GET / Get LAN Configuration Parameters to report; the rung is
// test.claim.machine_intake.machine_intake_bmc_served_lockout_witness.an_unread_threshold_refuses_the_failing_logins_a_served_one_admits.
fn bmc_lockout_reading_not_read(detail: NonEmptyStr, read_at: ObserverClockInstant) -> BmcControllerLockoutReading {
  bmc_lockout_reading(surfaces: [BmcLockoutSurfaceReading {
    surface: RedfishAccountServiceLogin,
    policy: LockoutPolicyNotReadable { cause: LockoutReadAttemptFailed { detail: detail } },
    evidence: bmc_lockout_absence_evidence(detail: detail),
    read_at: read_at,
  }], read_at: read_at)
}

// THE EVIDENCE OF A READ THAT DID NOT HAPPEN, labelled as such. It is not an
// EvidenceRef standing in for a receipt: its label says absence, and no code path
// turns it into a served property — the only thing it can produce is a refusal.
fn bmc_lockout_absence_evidence(detail: NonEmptyStr) -> EvidenceRef {
  EvidenceRef { label: join(["lockout-read-absent: ", detail], ""), digest: content_hash_of_value(value: join(["lockout-read-absent ", detail], "") as NonEmptyStr) }
}
